BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Salem Revolution250 Tour
DTSTART:20260417T000000
DTEND:20260927T000000
DTSTAMP:20260923T155014Z
UID:9d3c935639396b0c4ece57ed2a0d95@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Everyone knows Salem for the 1692 Witchcraft Trials\, but did 
 you know that Salem made significant contributions to the American Revolut
 ion? The shot heard round the world almost happened in Salem\, the town wa
 s known for its Privateers (legal Pirates) who were the most successful ag
 ainst the British Navy and British military governor General Thomas Gage e
 ncountered some of his biggest challenges to his authority in Salem. We al
 ways say that without Salem\, the United States may not be the same United
  States we know today. Come to Salem as part of the Rev250 Celebration and
  learn the incredible role our patriots played in the start of our country
 . Salem is a 30-minute ride from Boston on the Newburyport/Rockport train 
 from North Station (where the Bruins and Celtics play). There are late tra
 ins back to Boston after the tour. Come up for the day and take a morning 
 ferry to Salem and then the train back at night Our walking tours give you
  a wonderful perspective of our quaint city. We bring you throughout the d
 owntown area as well as the McIntire District. TOURS RUN RAIN OR SHINE. NO
  REFUNDS. We do not go inside any buildings\, dogs are allowed on our tour
 s\, with the exception of the cemetery and access to tour locations is sub
 ject to city regulations. A confirmation and details on meeting location i
 n Salem will be sent to you via email immediately after booking. CLICK HER
 E TO LEARN MORE\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https://www.meetbosto
 n.com/event/salem-revolution250-tour/88067/
LOCATION:Boston and Salem Walking Tours\, 8 Central Street\, Salem\, MA\, 
 01970
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/salem-revolution250-tour/88067/
END:VEVENT
