BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Memorial to Enslaved Persons
DTSTART:20260421T000000
DTEND:20260421T020000
DTSTAMP:20260923T155014Z
UID:6c095ece4c0a719a5994977e717526@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:On Sunday\, September 14th\, 2025\, King’s Chapel unveiled U
 nbound\, a memorial sculpture honoring the 219 children\, women\, and men 
 who were enslaved by past ministers and members of the church. This moment
  of truth-telling and remembrance marked an important step in our ongoing 
 commitment to reflection\, healing\, and reparative justice. Yet the unvei
 ling is only the beginning of our Living Memorial. We invite you to take p
 art in this journey. Join us for our new tour\, Journeying Through Freedom
  at 250 and experience the stories\, history\, and legacies that continue 
 to shape us today. You can also make a donation to help sustain the sculpt
 ure’s maintenance and support Living Memorial programs. Together\, we ca
 n honor the past while shaping a future grounded in truth\, healing\, and 
 community.\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https://www.meetboston.com
 /event/memorial-to-enslaved-persons/90242/
LOCATION:King’s Chapel\, King’s Chapel 58 Tremont Street\, Boston\, MA
 \, 02108
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/memorial-to-enslaved-persons/90242/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Visit Old West Church
DTSTART:20260421T000000
DTEND:20260421T020000
DTSTAMP:20260923T155014Z
UID:7b336844781a6925d087cc54da1adb@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Old West Church is the sixth home of the first congregation of
  the New England Conference of The United Methodist Church. Originally sit
 uated in Boston's North End and known as "Methodist Alley\," it later beca
 me the First Methodist Church in Boston. The building\, a registered "hist
 oric place" with the National Park Service\, was built in 1806 in the "mee
 ting house" architecture style by congregationalists. Once a safe house on
  the Underground Railroad prior to the Civil War\, the church is one of tw
 o post-colonial era buildings that survived the destruction of the West En
 d during the "urban renewal" of the 1950s. From 1896-1920\, the church ser
 ved as the West End Branch of the Boston Public Library. It was purchased 
 by Methodists from the city in 1962\, and became home to the congregation 
 of Old West Church. In 2023\, Old West Church joined the Union Combined Pa
 rish.\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https://www.meetboston.com/even
 t/visit-old-west-church/90240/
LOCATION:Old West Church\, Old West Church 131 Cambridge Street\, Boston\,
  MA\, 02114
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/visit-old-west-church/90240/
END:VEVENT
