BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The American Five
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260618
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260619
DTSTAMP:20260923T155014Z
UID:78e5aca03862f2810624864f57bd98@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Written by Chess Jakobs\, The American Five explores pivotal m
 oments in the lives of Dr. Martin Luther King Jr.\, Coretta Scott King\, B
 ayard Rustin\, Stanley Levison and Clarence B. Jones during the height of 
 the Civil Rights Movement. Set in the tense days leading up to the March o
 n Washington\, the play examines the strategy\, collaboration and moral co
 nviction behind one of the most consequential events in American history. 
 Developed through workshops at Ford’s Theatre and the University of Mich
 igan and premiering at Ford’s Theatre in September 2025\, this regional 
 premiere highlights themes of nonviolence\, leadership and personal sacrif
 ice while illuminating the immense pressure facing those who stood at the 
 forefront of change. In the face of government surveillance\, intimidation
 \, arrests and constant threats\, these five figures forged a coalition gr
 ounded in trust\, intellect and unwavering belief in justice.\n\nSources: 
 The Berkshires\nEvent page: https://berkshires.org/events-old/the-american
 -five/
LOCATION:Unicorn Theatre\, 6 East Street\, Stockbridge\, MA\, 01262
URL:https://berkshires.org/events-old/the-american-five/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Boston Witchcraft Tour
DTSTART:20260619T000000
DTEND:20260926T000000
DTSTAMP:20260923T155014Z
UID:99843741f5e34c4a55166d8897f127@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:The first witch execution in Boston was 1648 and four other wo
 men were executed for being witches over the next 40 years. Hear their sto
 ries and why they got accused. You’ll learn the story of Goody Glover\, 
 who was the last accused witch to be executed in Massachusetts before the 
 witchcraft hysteria erupted in Salem four years later that resulted in 25 
 deaths. This fascinating tour discusses witchcraft in Boston and some of t
 he Salem trials that spilled over to Boston involving Reverends Increase a
 nd Cotton Mather\, who played pivotal roles in the many of these witchcraf
 t accusations. You’ll learn about the hanging location\, where the victi
 ms lived\, who is interred in the cemetery\, see where the jail was locate
 d and more. This captivating tour will paint the picture of the colonial b
 elief that people could sign a pact with the devil and do harm to their ne
 ighbors with witchcraft. The meeting spot for this tour the Boston Common 
 Tablet at the corner of Park & Tremont Streets just steps from Park Street
  Subway Station. THIS TOUR IS IN BOSTON\, MASSACHUSETTS CLICK HERE TO PURC
 HASE TICKETS\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https://www.meetboston.c
 om/event/boston-witchcraft-tour/86479/
LOCATION:Boston and Salem Walking Tours\, Boston Common Tablet at the corn
 er of Park & Tremont Streets 1 Park Street Steps away from Park Street Sta
 tion\, Boston\, MA\, 02108
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/boston-witchcraft-tour/86479/
END:VEVENT
