UID:d57cf72e9c4491004232d277367712@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Boston conjures thoughts of Paul Revere\, the Boston Massacre
 \, and the start of the American Revolution. Take our walking tour and lea
 rn from a certified historian about these famous events that led to the bi
 rth of our nation. You'll also learn about Boston's humble beginnings in t
 he 1630s\, its growth through the 1600s\, and the colonial times of the 17
 00s. This fascinating tour will discuss many famous citizens\, Patriots\, 
 and events that molded the city of Boston through its first two centuries.
  You'll walk through history. You'll walk amongst old buildings. You'll wa
 lk in the footsteps of those who yearned to start a new country. This is a
  90-minute tour that will bring you to the Boston Common\, Granary Burying
  Grounds\, King's Chapel & Burying Grounds\, Government Center\, Court Squ
 are\, Boston Massacre Site and Faneuil Hall Marketplace. You will also pas
 s by many other locations. Tour details and meeting location will be sent 
 to you in a confirmation immediately you book the tour. LEARN MORE / GET T
 ICKETS\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https://www.meetboston.com/eve
 nt/boston-101%3a-historical-walking-tour/86282/
LOCATION:Boston and Salem Walking Tours\, The meeting spot for this tour i
 s between the Park Street Subway Station entrance and exit on the Boston C
 ommon near the corner of Tremont and Park Streets. Park & Tremont Streets
 \, Boston\, MA\, 02108
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/boston-101%3a-historical-walking-tour
 /86282/
