DTSTART:20260817T000000
DTEND:20260930T000000
DTSTAMP:20260923T155014Z
UID:2886d64cc53b120dd87b246fdc798b@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:From the JMAC: Submission Details Deadline: September 30\, 202
 6 @11:59 PM EST -- We invite artists and curators to submit proposals for 
 a fully conceptualized exhibition to be presented in conjunction with thea
 trical performances of Hedwig and the Angry Inch\, performed and produced 
 by The Hanover Theatre Repertory in the BrickBox Theatre. This exhibition 
 will be presented in the gallery\, outside the theater\, creating a dynami
 c\, interdisciplinary experience that bridges visual art and performance. 
 Selected proposals should present a cohesive and immersive exhibition conc
 ept that responds to and engages with the central themes of Hedwig and the
  Angry Inch. Artists are encouraged to interpret these themes broadly and 
 creatively. ​Thematic Focus Proposals must be rooted in themes inspired 
 by Hedwig and the Angry Inch\, including but not limited to: - Identity an
 d self-discovery - Transformation and reinvention - Gender\, queerness\, a
 nd fluidity - Love\, loss\, and longing - The body as a site of fragmentat
 ion and wholeness - Fame\, performance\, and persona - Resilience\, surviv
 al\, and personal mythology -- CLICK HERE TO LEARN MORE\n\nSources: Discov
 er Central Massachusetts\nEvent page: https://www.discovercentralma.org/ev
 ent/call-for-exhibition-proposals!/30662/
LOCATION:Jean McDonough Arts Center\, 20 Franklin St.\, Worcester\, MA\, 0
 1608
