BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sereening: Love\, Joy\, and Power: Tools for Liberation
DTSTART:20260920T000000
DTEND:20260923T000000
DTSTAMP:20260923T155014Z
UID:a8dbedcea60320d44626874fa9a4b6@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Follow the founders of Black Voters Matter as they empower Afr
 ican American voters to turn out in record-breaking numbers\, flipping Geo
 rgia blue in 2020 despite dangerous threats. In the face of today’s powe
 rful attempts at voter suppression\, their vital\, brave story sheds keen 
 light on the work that still remains to be done for America to make good o
 n its promise of democracy for all. Come see the film and join a community
  conversation. Three screenings in September\, admission free. Registratio
 n recommended: SCHEDULE Sunday\, Sept. 20\, 3:00pm at Just Bookish Monday
 \, Sept 21\, 5:30pm at Boston Public Library\, Shaw-Roxbury Branch Wednesd
 ay\, Sept. 23\, 6:30pm at Mass College of Art & Design Community Sponsors 
 include: Black History in Action\, Boston Public Library\, Shaw-Roxbury Br
 anch\, Dunamis Boston\, JP Progressives\, Just Bookish\, Meraki Production
 s (list in formation). LEARN MORE / REGISTER TODAY\n\nSources: Meet Boston
