BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mariachi El Bronx
DTSTART:20260923T000000
DTEND:20260923T000000
DTSTAMP:20260923T155014Z
UID:eaae434aa81216217c99bc09ceca0f@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Ten years after their last run\, the alter ego of punk heroes 
 The Bronx returns to the stage in full charro suits\, trading distortion f
 or trumpet and violin without losing an ounce of the intensity. Eight musi
 cians deep\, the band treats mariachi and punk as the same instinct wearin
 g different clothes\, both rooted in working class storytelling\, both bui
 lt to move a room. Expect galloping rhythms\, hallucinogenic violin lines
 \, and a horn section that hits like a gut punch\, pulled from a catalog t
 hat's carried the band from Coachella to Letterman's stage. New material f
 rom Mariachi El Bronx IV threads through the set\, songs written in the sp
 ace between grief and getting married\, between wildfire and wedding vows.
  Live\, that tension turns into something closer to catharsis\, a set that
  swings from hard-won hope to full-throated celebration and back again. LE
 ARN MORE / GET TICKETS\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https://www.me
 etboston.com/event/mariachi-el-bronx/93088/
LOCATION:City Winery Boston\, City Winery 80 Beverly Street\, Boston\, MA
 \, 02114
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/mariachi-el-bronx/93088/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Meet author Miciah Bay Gault and Melissa Febos
DTSTART:20260923T000000
DTEND:20260923T000000
DTSTAMP:20260923T155014Z
UID:9488ffec91f0ffa43454f5141adfb4@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Author Talk with Miciah Bay Gault & Melissa Febos Join us Wedn
 esday\, September 23 at 4 p.m. at West Falmouth Library to meet Miciah Bay
  Gault for an author talk and special opportunity to purchase a signed cop
 y of The Nobody Code\, in partnership with Eight Cousins Bookstore. Also i
 n attendance will be guest speaker Melissa Febos\, author of The Dry Seaso
 n: A Memoir. Melissa’s books will also be for sale at this event. Free a
 nd open to all. On The Nobody Code: A spellbinding novel steeped in New En
 gland folklore following a woman who leaves her marriage to uncover who’
 s punishing her for the crimes of her adolescence—for fans of Liz Moore
 ’s The God of the Woods and Celeste Ng’s Everything I Never Told You. 
 “Gault explores coming-of-age\, the power of stories\, and vigilante jus
 tice in this ambitious literary mystery. . . . [She] dusts the proceedings
  with light mysticism . . . grounding the story’s emotional stakes while
  lending it added psychological depth. . . . Engrossing.”―Publisher’
 s Weekly On The Dry Season: A Memoir: From Melissa Febos\, the national be
 stselling author of Girlhood\, comes an examination of the solitude\, free
 doms\, and feminist heroes she discovered during a year of celibacy and a 
 wise and transformative look at relationships and self-knowledge. “The D
 ry Season is a propulsive\, thoughtful memoir about the author’s yearlon
 g hiatus from dating\, romance\, and sex. . . . In a culture obsessed with
  love and sex\, where being single is pathologized and looked down upon\, 
 this story of solo self-discovery is revolutionary.”—Oprah Daily “Pr
 esenting a model for celibacy that is self-guided rather than socially imp
 osed and compassionate rather than punitive\; this book should be required
  reading for anyone who’s ever been told to ‘just take a break from re
 lationships.’”—Vogue Register Here\n\nSources: Cape Cod Chamber\nEve
 nt page: https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/meet-author-miciah-bay-gault
 -and-melissa-febos/52323/
LOCATION:West Falmouth Library\, 575 West Falmouth Highway\, West Falmouth
 \, MA\, 02574
URL:https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/meet-author-miciah-bay-gault-and-
 melissa-febos/52323/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Midnight in The War Room
DTSTART:20260923T000000
DTEND:20260923T000000
DTSTAMP:20260923T155014Z
UID:5aaf5971ec35f3b218a18e03968033@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Midnight in the War Room isn’t just a documentary. It’s a 
 call to action. Featuring more than 50 experts\, the film brings together 
 voices that rarely share the same stage: global CISOs\, reformed hackers\,
  military strategists\, cyber psychologists\, journalists\, and victims. T
 heir perspectives collide to expose one truth…time is running out. We’
 re standing at the breaking point of a digital arms race. Nation states\, 
 criminal syndicates\, and rogue actors are exploiting critical systems fas
 ter than we can secure them. The defenders holding the line are exhausted 
 — yet they keep going\, because the stakes aren’t theoretical. In some
  cases\, they’re life or death. This film isn’t just about bits and by
 tes. It’s about humanity. It’s about what happens when trust becomes a
  target and complacency becomes a weapon. Cyber war isn’t science fictio
 n. It’s here now. And\, the outcome depends on all of us. The clock is t
 icking. LEARN MORE / GET TICKETS\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: http
 s://www.meetboston.com/event/midnight-in-the-war-room/93279/
LOCATION:AMC Theatre\, AMC Theatre Stoughton 217 Washington Street\, Stoug
 hton\, MA\, 02072
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/midnight-in-the-war-room/93279/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Nature Walk at the Shipyard
DTSTART:20260923T110000
DTEND:20260923T120000
DTSTAMP:20260923T155014Z
