SUMMARY:Strange Land
DTSTART:20260923T000000
DTEND:20260923T000000
DTSTAMP:20260923T155014Z
UID:5f0bde76bd1af3b6ea31f082d5ed03@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:The Museum of Science welcomes Nightingale\, in collaboration 
 with Juventas New Music Ensemble\, composer Gregory W. Brown\, visual arti
 st Brian D. Cohen\, and poet Todd Hearon\, for the premiere of Strange Lan
 d — an immersive multimedia experience that reimagines the Book of Revel
 ation through a modern lens\, exploring the collision of ancient spiritual
  questions with our technological present. The score sets modern and ancie
 nt psalms for choir\, tenor soloist\, and chamber ensemble\, augmented wit
 h electronic sound. The performance is paired with monumental imagery: etc
 hings on copper plates\, printed by hand in the traditional manner\, then 
 enlarged to colossal scale and projected in vivid detail across the IMAX s
 creen. Join us for a profound\, embodied\, and reflective evening. Perform
 ers: Nightingale Vocal Ensemble with Juventas New Music Ensemble Conductor
 : Ben Perry Music: Gregory W. Brown Text: Todd Hearon\, from Strange Land 
 (2010)\, and scripture Artwork: Brian D. Cohen\, from De Profundis (2026) 
 LEARN MORE / GET TICKETS\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https://www.
 meetboston.com/event/strange-land/93017/
LOCATION:Museum of Science\, Museum of Science 1 Science Park\, Boston\, M
 A\, 02114
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/strange-land/93017/
END:VEVENT
