BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Afterglow at the Arnold
DTSTART:20260924T000000
DTEND:20260924T000000
DTSTAMP:20260923T155014Z
UID:a123c1fb8531271986448e79e94807@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Join us at the Arnold Arboretum as we debut a captivating new 
 event: Afterglow at the Arnold! This enchanting evening of discovery under
  the stars celebrates the Arboretum as a free public park in the City of B
 oston\, a “museum of trees\,” a conservation and research institution
 \, and a community resource for education and well-being. The event will b
 e hosted in our Arnold Arboretum’s Explorers Garden on Bussey Hill\, whe
 re plants collected from around the world are cultivated to support the st
 udy and preservation of biodiversity. Guests will engage with Arboretum ex
 perts while enjoying cocktails and passed food in the living collections\,
  followed by music and dancing under a tent. Afterglow at the Arnold start
 s at 5:30pm with a VIP experience for guests to interact with Arboretum le
 adership and draw from their vast knowledge of the Arboretum and its colle
 ctions. Guests can mingle and enjoy food and drinks while the sun sets and
  our trees are illuminated. The exclusive VIP experience runs until 7:30pm
 \, but VIP ticket holders are welcome and encouraged to stay the entire ev
 ening\, and especially for the speaking remarks at 8:15pm. This event is p
 resented with the Young Friends at the Arnold\, our friends group designed
  to inspire supporters aged 21-45 (and anyone young at heart) to engage mo
 re deeply with the Arboretum and the natural world. Guests purchasing a Yo
 ung Friends ticket are invited to join the event from 7:30-10:30pm\, featu
 ring passed food\, drinks\, music\, and content stations will be available
  for the rest of the evening. Event Details 5:30–7:30pm — Afterglow VI
 P Experience Hearty bites and food stations Specialty cocktail/mocktail Sp
 ecial content with Arboretum leaders 8:15pm — Speaking program for all a
 ttendees Brief remarks and presentation from Arboretum Director 7:30–10:
 30pm — Afterparty / Young Friends Passed food and an open wine and beer 
 bar Content tables with staff experts Live band and dancing LEARN MORE / B
 UY TICKETS\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https://www.meetboston.com
 /event/afterglow-at-the-arnold/92988/
LOCATION:Arnold Arboretum\, Jamaica Plain\, Arnold Arboretum 1300 Centre S
 treet\, Jamaica Plain\, MA
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/afterglow-at-the-arnold/92988/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Andris Nelsons conducts Mahler Symphony No. 7
DTSTART:20260924T000000
DTEND:20260926T000000
DTSTAMP:20260923T155014Z
UID:e27e04bb753e8883a5ef5e765407a0@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:One of the great composers of the past century\, the Russian-b
 orn Sofia Gubaidulina infused her intricate\, penetrating music with deep 
 spirituality. A frequent collaborator with the BSO and Andris Nelsons\, sh
 e was composing her Prologue \, a BSO co-commission with the Gewandhausorc
 hester Leipzig\, when she died\; the eminent Russian composer Elena Firsov
 a has completed it for performance. Gustav Mahler’s Seventh Symphony\, a
 n intense orchestral journey with moments of sardonic humor\, begins sombe
 rly and ends in glorious triumph. The Seventh is the only Mahler symphony 
 Andris Nelsons has yet to conduct with the BSO. LEARN MORE / GET TICKETS\n
 \nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https://www.meetboston.com/event/andri
 s-nelsons-conducts-mahler-symphony-no-7/93070/
