BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ballet Magnificat! Anchored: The Pilgrim Story
DTSTART:20260925T000000
DTEND:20260925T000000
DTSTAMP:20260923T155014Z
UID:c997ec0c044df73541106f65df413b@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:In honor of America’s 250th Anniversary\, Ballet Magnificat!
  brings Anchored: The Pilgrim Story to Massachusetts. Beautifully choreogr
 aphed\, Anchored inspires audiences today with its portrayal of the courag
 e and faith of the Pilgrims\, their perilous crossing\, and their friendsh
 ip which developed with Native Americans. Their legacy of religious freedo
 m\, individual responsibility\, and equality of all people helped prepare 
 the way for America’s independence. Passion\, artistry\, heartfelt worsh
 ip and technical excellence define Ballet Magnificat!’s performances. Th
 e Company artists have graced stages of theaters\, opera houses\, concert 
 halls\, and church auditoriums throughout America and Europe with their po
 werful portrayal of redemptive themes\, inspired by true-life stories. Anc
 hored: The Pilgrim Story is an original work created to honor the 400th An
 niversary of the Pilgrims and their lasting legacy which informed our Foun
 ding Fathers and the Declaration of Independence. The libretto for the Pil
 grim Ballet was carefully researched and written by a direct descendant of
  William Bradford\, and beautifully choreographed and set to music by Ball
 et Magnificat! The groundbreaking beliefs of the Pilgrims in freedom and e
 quality of all people before God and under the law are vividly apparent in
  this dramatic and moving rendition of the Pilgrim story. This performance
  is presented by FirstLoveWorks\, a nonprofit organization\, which hosts e
 xceptional arts performances that offer the general public opportunities t
 o experience the majesty and love of God. We have produced three tours of 
 Ballet Magnifcat!\, including one at Mechanics Hall over 20 years ago. It
 ’s our pleasure to once again bring the Ballet to Worcester to commemora
 te America’s 250th Anniversary. Ballet Magnificat! takes its name from M
 ary's song of praise recorded in Luke 1\, where she exclaims\, "My soul ma
 gnifies the Lord\, and my spirit rejoices in God my Savior." Kathy Thibode
 aux\, a world-class ballerina who won a silver medal in the II USA Interna
 tional Ballet Competition\, founded the Company in 1986 as a means whereby
  she could combine her love of dance with her profound Christian faith. He
 r husband Keith Thibodeaux became the Executive Director in 1993\; a child
 -prodigy himself\, he first stepped into the limelight as "Little Ricky" i
 n the "I Love Lucy" show. Today the Company has a fully developed training
  and internship program\, workshops\, and two touring companies\, which to
 ur regularly overseas in addition to within the U.S. Based in Jackson\, MS
 \, they have also established a professional trainee program and performan
 ce company headquartered in Curitiba\, Brazil.\n\nSources: Discover Centra
 l Massachusetts\nEvent page: https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/balle
 t-magnificat!-anchored%3a-the-pilgrim-story/30403/
LOCATION:Mechanics Hall\, 321 Main St.\, Worcester\, MA\, 01608
URL:https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/ballet-magnificat!-anchored%3a
 -the-pilgrim-story/30403/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Beethoven's Tango
DTSTART:20260925T000000
DTEND:20260927T000000
DTSTAMP:20260923T155014Z
UID:f8eac673199ced2290bc1456e15cc0@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Featuring an original score by Latin Grammy artists Alfredo Mi
 netti & Richard Scofano\, Beethoven’s Tango celebrates the composer’s 
 relentless drive to create. The show invites the audience to meet Beethove
 n during his most private struggle\, incubated in solitude\, forged by des
 ire\, resilience\, revelation\, and unstoppable creative force. Classical 
 music and Argentine tango intertwine\, not as fusion but as tension: they 
 confront\, resist\, and transform one another. Embodied by tango dancers\,
  music and movement combine to access the depth of the human struggle behi
 nd the composer’s mind— how to offer music while descending into a wor
 ld of increasing deafness. The work asserts that the creative urge does no
 t belong solely to artists\, nor to any single tradition or culture. It is
  instead a latent force within all human beings: a creative pulse capable 
 of restoring depth\, meaning\, and presence in a world increasingly flatte
 ned by speed\, consumption\, and spectacle. FRI SEP 25 7:30pm SAT SEP 26 7
 :30pm Sun SEP 27 3:00pm Unleashing the Duende\, a 2-hour guided workshop o
 n Sep 23rd\, proposes a return to authorship rooted in risk. It invites us
  to recognize ourselves within this struggle\, and to encounter our own Du
 ende: the inner force that resists\, creates\, and insists on expression o
 f uncompromising authenticity. LEARN MORE / GET TICKETS\n\nSources: Meet B
 oston\nEvent page: https://www.meetboston.com/event/beethovens-tango/93111
 /
LOCATION:MIT Kresge Theater\, 48 Massachusetts Avenue\, Cambridge MA\, 48 
 Massachusetts Avenue\, Cambridge\, MA\, 02139
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/beethovens-tango/93111/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cape Cod Pottery Trail
DTSTART:20260925T000000
DTEND:20260927T000000
DTSTAMP:20260923T155014Z
UID:7cc0bf95d8965937393dd7a6b757f4@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Travel the Trail: September 26-27th\, 10am - 4pm Preview Party
 : September 25\, 5-7pm Ready\, Set\, Go! Join us for the 2nd annual Cape C
 od Pottery Trail! This self-guided trail offers a rare behind-the-scenes l
 ook at the people and places where Cape Cod pottery is made. With 16 locat
 ions on the 2026 map and multiple artists at some locations\, visitors can
  experience an extraordinary range of ceramic work—from wheel-thrown and
  slipcast functional ware to hand-built sculpture\, jewelry\, raku and woo
 d-fired pieces. Many of these spaces are not open to the public outside th
 e Trail\, making the weekend a unique opportunity to meet the artists\, se
 e their creative processes\, and purchase work directly from the makers. T
 he Trail is free and open to everyone.There is no starting point or route.
  Visitors already on-Cape can jump onto the trail at any location\, while 
 those arriving from off-Cape often begin at the Sagamore location. Downloa
 d a map from the PotteryTrail website. For an added element of fun\, this 
 map doubles as a Pottery Passport which provides space to collect a stamp 
 at each stop. Complete the passport and turn it in at the final stop for a
  chance to win a handmade piece created by one of the Trail artists. Kick 
 Off the Weekend at the Preview Party The weekend begins with a preview par
 ty on Friday\, September 25\, from 5–7 p.m. at Brick Kiln Farm in Falmou
 th. Tickets for the reception are $10\, offering guests an opportunity to 
 preview the work and meet participating artists before setting out on the 
 trail. For ticket purchases\, the artist roster\, download the Pottery Pas
 sport\, and additional information\, visit capecodpotterytrail.com.\n\nSou
 rces: Cape Cod Chamber\nEvent page: https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/c
 ape-cod-pottery-trail/51865/
LOCATION:Perch Pottery\, Falmouth\, MA\, 02536
URL:https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/cape-cod-pottery-trail/51865/
END:VEVENT
