SUMMARY:September Happenings at 65 Water Street\, Newburyport!
DTSTART:20260925T110000
DTEND:20261012T170000
DTSTAMP:20260923T155014Z
UID:61561f1face2e0055d28115e4d66b4@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Newburyport Art (NAA): see what’s happening at 65 Water Stre
 et in September. It’s the month to start learning more! Details and regi
 strations are found at Newburyportart.org/classes-and-workshops Art Market
  behind 65 Water Street\, Sunday\, September 13th\, 11am-3pm Join NAA memb
 ers for the final arts market in the outdoor sculpture garden. Participati
 ng artists: Kallyn Lavallee\, Patrick Cleary\, Lisa Pilorz\, Lynda Hartwel
 l\, Elizabeth Wiltshire Daylight Drawing: Sunday\, September 13th\, 1pm-2:
 30pm Come & draw fellow artists\, plus take turns posing for the group! Al
 l skill levels are welcome\, and you’ll need to bring your own materials
 . FREE of charge! Wednesday Night Live Drawing Sessions: September 16th\, 
 23rd & 30th\, 6:30-8:30pm Our weekly Life Drawing Sessions offer artists t
 he opportunity to draw from a live model in non-instructionals sessions fa
 cilitated by Claudia Mathews. The model will pose in several positions for
  both short and long poses. Artists should bring their own materials. Sess
 ions are in the Hartson Gallery\, which is only accessible by stairs. Regi
 ster online or walk-in. $12 for NAA Members/$15 for Non-Members Intro to S
 poon Carving with Eric Goodson: Saturday\, September 19th\, 9am-4pm Learn 
 about wood selection\, grain orientation\, spoon design\, ergonomics and a
  wide variety of knife grips that make carving fast\, efficient & safe. Er
 ic will discuss finishing oils\, paint & decorative techniques. Loaner too
 ls will be available\, or students can bring their own carving tools. No e
 xperience necessary. $95 for NAA Members/$125 for Non-Members Artist Talk:
  The Unlaunched Cartooning Career of John Updike\, September 26th\, 6-8pm 
 Join Michael Updike to talk about his father’s cartoons and him becoming
  a two-time Pulitzer Prize-winning novelist. FREE to NAA Members/$10 for N
 on-Members. Registration required. Gallery Hours: Wednesday through Sunday
  from 11am-5pm. The gallery is handicap accessible. More information\, as 
 well as an online gallery is available at newburyportart.org. Founded in 1
 948\, Newburyport Art is dedicated to promoting and exhibiting members’ 
 work and to providing art education and access to the visual arts for the 
 entire community.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northof
 boston.org/event/september-happenings-at-65-water-street-newburyport/2026-
 09-25/
LOCATION:Newburyport Art Association\, 65 Water St\, Newburyport\, MA\, 01
 950
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/september-happenings-at-65-water-stree
 t-newburyport/2026-09-25/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Terry Fator
DTSTART:20260925T000000
DTEND:20260925T000000
DTSTAMP:20260923T155014Z
UID:2ddd2a977be62daa36b8fa7af72ac4@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Legendary Las Vegas headliner Terry Fator has created a new ro
 ad show to kickoff his 2025-2026 tour. Pure Imagination: Once Upon a Voice
  is a 90 minute spectacular\, featuring the incredible impressions\, comed
 y and ventriloquism that has made Terry and his characters a must see show
  for fans across the nation. “Pure Imagination is a totally different co
 ncept than my road shows in the past\,” Fator said. “I found that thro
 ughout my life my imagination had spawned countless characters\, song paro
 dies and comedy skits and I compiled them all together to give my audience
  a fun look into my creative psyche.” The show features the classic char
 acters Terry has made famous over the years: Winston the Impersonating Tur
 tle\; Country Star Walter T. Airdale\; Apollo Theater legend Julius\; perp
 etual slacker and stoner Duggie\; Vikki the Cougar and the world’s great
 est Elvis impersonator\, Maynard Tompkins. “One idea I had is to add in 
 characters and impressions based on real-life stars people around the worl
 d know and love\,” Fator said. “So you can look forward to seeing and 
 hearing Willie Nelson\, Michael Jackson\, Justin Bieber\, plus a few surpr
 ise ‘guests’”. Simply put\, Pure Imagination is Pure Entertainment f
 or audiences across the country.\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: http
 s://www.meetboston.com/event/terry-fator/90607/
LOCATION:Chevalier Theatre\, 30 Forest Street\, Medford\, MA\, 02155
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/terry-fator/90607/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The NAA invites you to the 25th Annual Art Auction Exhibition & Ev
 ent
DTSTART:20260925T110000
DTEND:20261027T170000
DTSTAMP:20260923T155014Z
UID:4f9929a49075dae5edb55724599d35@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Newburyport Art (NAA) invites artists\, members\, collectors\,
  friends\, and art lovers to gather for a celestial celebration of 25 year
 s of creativity\, connection\, and community. This year’s Art Auction ex
 hibition is on display from Wednesday\, September 2nd until Saturday\, Oct
 ober 3rd. A ticketed auction party will be held on Saturday\, October 3rd
 \, from 4-8pm. Over 160 artworks are available for online silent auction b
 idding now until October 3rd @6pm. In the downstairs Sargent Gallery\, the
  exhibit includes NAA Member Artwork featuring photography\, mixed media\,
  sculpture\, oil\, acrylic and more. Upstairs in the Hartson Gallery is th
 e Collector’s Collection – showcasing artwork donated from private col
 lections\, including work by notable artists such as Harold Feinstein\, Ca
 ra Weston\, and Carlos Mérida. For online bidding & tickets to our Octobe
 r 3rd party\, visit: Auctria.events./NewburyportArt25 Since 1948\, Newbury
 port Art has believed in the power of art to bring people together. For on
 e unforgettable event\, Saturday\, October 3rd\, from 4-8pm\, 65 Water Str
 eet will transform into a celebratory theme of a black\, white and silver 
 sky. The afternoon and evening offers a variety of ways to experience the 
 celebration including: live painting by Alan Bull and a chance to purchase
  his piece\; bidding on Members’ Artwork\, Collectors Collection\, and S
 ilent Auction Packages\; adding your own star and to an interactive commun
 ity constellation\; free tarot reading\; dancing to live jazz & swing with
  Jared Holaday\; sipping on a signature cocktail from the open bar\; enjoy
 ing catered food and dessert\; posing for your Moon Portrait in the sculpt
 ure garden\; and sharing your NAA story in an optional two-minute video in
 terview. NAA Member tickets: $70\; Non-member tickets: $90\; with a sugges
 ted attire of cosmic shine! Thank you to our lead sponsors\, Matter Commun
 ications\, Milestone 35 Tools & Woodworking\, and the Hylton Family Trust 
 for supporting our 25th Annual Art Auction. Gallery Hours: Wednesday throu
 gh Sunday from 11:00am–5:00pm. The gallery is handicap accessible. More 
 information\, as well as an online gallery is available at newburyportart.
 org.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/ev
 ent/the-naa-invites-you-to-the-25th-annual-art-auction-exhibition-event/20
 26-09-25/
LOCATION:Newburyport Art Association\, 65 Water St\, Newburyport\, MA\, 01
 950
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/the-naa-invites-you-to-the-25th-annual
 -art-auction-exhibition-event/2026-09-25/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tinlicker
DTSTART:20260925T000000
DTEND:20260925T000000
DTSTAMP:20260923T155014Z
UID:c1c9a7d112c59230d636de2bade6b8@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Over more than a decade\, Tinlicker have consistently pushed b
 oundaries in the world of electronic music\, cultivating a sound that is b
 oth unique and personal. The use of real instruments\, ranging from string
 s to keys to horns\, has long been a staple of the ensemble that helps to 
 separate their sound from more traditional dance acts. Beyond the instrume
 ntation\, their music also has an unusual and powerful propensity to evoke
  an array of feelings\, from euphoria to sadness\, and everything in betwe
 en. It’s music one can dance to\, no doubt\, but it’s also music that 
 tells a compelling story. After their 2021 breakthrough with single ‘Bec
 ause You Move Me’ (over 1 billion streams now)\, Tinlicker implemented s
 ome radical changes - they left their long-time label\, Anjunadeep for [PI
 AS] and transitioned from performing purely DJ sets to a format including 
 live/band performances. Risky but well-calculated choices\, necessary for 
 the next steps to realize the creative direction of the album they were wo
 rking on\, ‘Cold Enough For Snow’ (2024). The resulting LP was a maste
 rclass in balancing innovation with quality. Reroute to remain.\n\nSources
 : Meet Boston\nEvent page: https://www.meetboston.com/event/tinlicker/9322
 6/
LOCATION:Roadrunner\, 89 Guest Street Boston Landing\, Brighton\, MA\, 021
 35
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/tinlicker/93226/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Trey Hensley
DTSTART:20260925T193000
DTEND:20260925T210000
DTSTAMP:20260923T155014Z
UID:641d1a92364c570a35a9a8b468e94b@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:GRAMMY® winner and reigning two-time IBMA Guitar Player of th
 e Year Trey Hensley has been called a “musical phenom” by NPR\, “a g
 uitar-slinging superhero” by Bluegrass Today\, “Nashville’s hottest 
 young player” by Acoustic Guitar magazine\, and “the Swiss Army knife 
 of roots music” by WMOT Radio’s Craig Havighurst. Hensley’s artistry
  has received high praise from the likes of Merle Haggard and Marty Stuart
 . An Eric Clapton’s Crossroads Guitar Festival invitee who has collabora
 ted with Johnny Cash\, Vince Gill\, Dolly Parton\, Taj Mahal and Tommy Emm
 anuel\, Hensley is known for his other-worldly guitar playing\, jaw-droppi
 ng musicianship and soulful storytelling. Having recently announced his si
 gnature guitar with Taylor Guitars: The Trey Hensley Gold Label 510e\, Hen
 sley is set to release a new album\, Can’t Outrun The Blues\, on March 6
 \, 2026. The title cut has spent multiple weeks at #1 on the bluegrass cha
 rts.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/ev
 ent/trey-hensley/
LOCATION:Shalin Liu Performance Center\, 37 Main Street\, Rockport\, MA\, 
 01966
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/trey-hensley/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Worcester Chamber Music Society Concert: Autumn Winds - Harvard
DTSTART:20260925T000000
DTEND:20260925T000000
DTSTAMP:20260923T155014Z
UID:4612067f269ad3b9d1e332e9ef2373@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Autumn Winds We open the season with three pieces written in t
 hree centuries. Mozart and Brahms each composed works in their masterful s
 tyles that display the virtuosity of the hornist and clarinetist for whom 
 they were written. Dohnányi’s Sextet showcases both instruments in a wo
 rk that nods to Brahms while delighting in its own eccentricity and sass. 
 Friday\, September 25 @7:30 PM Unitarian Universalist Church 9 Ayer Road\,
  Harvard Pre-concert talk @7:00 PM Program Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart: Horn Q
 uintet in E-flat major\, K.407/386c Johannes Brahms: Clarinet Trio\, Op. 1
 14 Ernő Dohnányi: Sextet\, Op. 37 With guests Gary Gorczyca\, clarinet /
  Clark Matthews\, horn This performance is funded in part by the Shirley C
 ultural Council\, a local agency funded by the Massachusetts Cultural Coun
 cil\, a state agency. venue is handicapped accessible\n\nSources: Discover
  Central Massachusetts\nEvent page: https://www.discovercentralma.org/even
 t/worcester-chamber-music-society-concert%3a-autumn-winds-harvard/30757/
LOCATION:Worcester Chamber Music Society\, 9 Ayer Road\, Harvard\, MA\, 01
 451
URL:https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/worcester-chamber-music-societ
 y-concert%3a-autumn-winds-harvard/30757/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Yin Yu Tang: A Chinese Home Tour
DTSTART:20260925T111500
DTEND:20260925T161500
DTSTAMP:20260923T155014Z
UID:5afefa07cdf7b4db9026f9398d6e1b@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Step inside a 200-year-old Chinese home in Salem to experience
  Chinese art\, architecture and culture. For 200 years\, Yin Yu Tang stood
  in the rural village of Huang Cun in a mountainous region of southeastern
  China. Home to eight generations of the Huang family\, this house was dis
 mantled\, transported and re-erected at the Peabody Essex Museum in 2003 t
 hrough a partnership between PEM and the governmental authorities of Huizh
 ou\, in Anhui Province. Yin Yu Tang’s journey constitutes a landmark col
 laboration between Chinese and American architects\, artisans\, conservato
 rs\, engineers and museum experts. The home is presented as it was when th
 e family last lived there in 1982. Plan Your Visit Exercise care Please he
 lp us preserve the house for future generations by refraining from touchin
 g objects and the structure itself. Non-flash photography and videography 
 is permitted for personal use only. Tripods and selfie sticks are not allo
 wed. Please walk with care and watch out for uneven stonework and raised t
 hresholds. Store your belongings\, but keep your coat Yin Yu Tang is parti
 ally outdoors and may be cool in fall and winter. Strollers\, bags\, backp
 acks and umbrellas are not permitted in the house. Please leave them at th
 e coatroom or the cubbies by the Information desk. Our staff at the entran
 ce of the house can look after strollers. Pick up your audio guide in adva
 nce Please pick up your complimentary audio guide\, available in English a
 nd Mandarin\, at the Information desk 10 minutes before your visit. Please
  note: Plan to bring your own pair of headphones. Before your visit\, pres
 s #50 to listen to an introduction to the house. Once inside\, look for st
 one blocks with two-digit numbers. Press the number plus the play > button
  to hear the audio. Be prompt Please be at the doors to Yin Yu Tang five m
 inutes before your scheduled visit with your audio guide in hand. A staff 
 member will alert you shortly before the end of your time slot.\n\nSources
 : North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/event/yin-yu-tang
 -a-chinese-home-tour/2026-09-25/
LOCATION:Peabody Essex Museum\, East India Square\, 161 Essex Street\, Sal
 em\, MA\, 01970
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/yin-yu-tang-a-chinese-home-tour/2026-0
 9-25/
END:VEVENT
