BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cambridge Explores the Universe 2026
DTSTART:20260926T000000
DTEND:20260926T000000
DTSTAMP:20260923T155014Z
UID:abefec7163b4fac9a2f802692566af@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Do you wonder how astronomers and astrophysicists unravel the 
 mysteries of our universe? Now’s your chance to find out! The Center for
  Astrophysics | Harvard & Smithsonian is excited to announce that their an
 nual FREE family-friendly open house\, Cambridge Explores the Universe\, i
 s back on Saturday September 26th from 12 to 4 pm. Come dive into our late
 st discoveries from across the Universe! Visitors to this family-friendly 
 open house can enjoy hands-on exploration stations and opportunities to as
 k our scientists all of your burning questions about space. There will be 
 activities such as: Solar observing Taking telescope images with robotic t
 elescopes Celestial Navigation Behind the scenes telescope tours Gravity w
 ell And much much more! Chat with our astronomers and astrophysicists acro
 ss the observatory on topics such as black holes\, the Sun\, air pollution
 \, exoplanets\, and more. You don’t want to miss this “out of this wor
 ld” experience! Register for free here! About the Center for Astrophysic
 s: The Center for Astrophysics | Harvard & Smithsonian is a collaboration 
 between Harvard and Smithsonian designed to ask — and ultimately answer 
 — humanity’s greatest unresolved questions about the nature of the uni
 verse. Founded in 1973\, the CfA has sought to foster innovation and prope
 l discovery across the universe. Today\, CfA is the largest astronomy orga
 nization in the world. The CfA is dedicated to exploring\, understanding a
 nd sharing the wonder of the universe with all who look up at the night sk
 y and ask: What’s out there? *Some activities and behind-the-scenes acce
 ss have limited capacity. The Center for Astrophysics | Harvard & Smithson
 ian welcomes visitors of all ages and abilities. LEARN MORE / GET TICKETS
 \n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https://www.meetboston.com/event/cam
 bridge-explores-the-universe-2026/92765/
LOCATION:Center for Astrophysics\, Center for Astrophysics 60 Garden St\, 
 Cambridge\, MA\, 02138
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/cambridge-explores-the-universe-2026/
 92765/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cape Cod Pottery Trail
DTSTART:20260926T000000
DTEND:20260927T000000
DTSTAMP:20260923T155014Z
UID:74002fd7f4b1375908cb96fd878e5c@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Travel the Trail: September 26-27th\, 10am - 4pm Preview Party
 : September 25\, 5-7pm Ready\, Set\, Go! Join us for the 2nd annual Cape C
 od Pottery Trail! This self-guided trail offers a rare behind-the-scenes l
 ook at the people and places where Cape Cod pottery is made. With 16 locat
 ions on the 2026 map and multiple artists at some locations\, visitors can
  experience an extraordinary range of ceramic work—from wheel-thrown and
  slipcast functional ware to hand-built sculpture\, jewelry\, raku and woo
 d-fired pieces. Many of these spaces are not open to the public outside th
 e Trail\, making the weekend a unique opportunity to meet the artists\, se
 e their creative processes\, and purchase work directly from the makers. T
 he Trail is free and open to everyone.There is no starting point or route.
  Visitors already on-Cape can jump onto the trail at any location\, while 
 those arriving from off-Cape often begin at the Sagamore location. Downloa
 d a map from the PotteryTrail website. For an added element of fun\, this 
 map doubles as a Pottery Passport which provides space to collect a stamp 
 at each stop. Complete the passport and turn it in at the final stop for a
  chance to win a handmade piece created by one of the Trail artists. Kick 
 Off the Weekend at the Preview Party The weekend begins with a preview par
 ty on Friday\, September 25\, from 5–7 p.m. at Brick Kiln Farm in Falmou
 th. Tickets for the reception are $10\, offering guests an opportunity to 
 preview the work and meet participating artists before setting out on the 
 trail. For ticket purchases\, the artist roster\, download the Pottery Pas
 sport\, and additional information\, visit capecodpotterytrail.com.\n\nSou
 rces: Cape Cod Chamber\nEvent page: https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/c
 ape-cod-pottery-trail/52459/
LOCATION:254 Brick Kiln Road\, Falmouth\, MA\, 02536
URL:https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/cape-cod-pottery-trail/52459/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cape Symphony: The Planets
DTSTART:20260926T000000
DTEND:20260927T000000
DTSTAMP:20260923T155014Z
UID:c0f5b00f7ed681c18035b52453a7a4@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:As we open a bold new season of discovery\, we invite you on a
  thrilling journey beyond the horizon. From the vastness of the cosmos to 
 the wonder of the unknown\, this spectacular opening concert launches Worl
 ds Await with music that is thrilling\, cinematic\, and awe-inspiring. We
 ’ll begin in orbit\, with Kaija Saariaho’s radiant meditation on the m
 otion of the cosmos. Prokofiev’s Violin Concerto No. 1 follows\, balanci
 ng dreamlike lyricism with flashes of wit. The journey culminates in Holst
 ’s The Planets \, a suite of vivid astrological portraits from martial t
 hunder to shimmering mysticism. Ticketholders are invited to an entertaini
 ng and informative talk about the concert program given by trombonist and 
 scholar George Scharr beginning one hour before the performance. Alyssa Wa
 ng\, Conductor Nathan Olson\, Violin Program: KAIJA SAARIAHO Asteroid 4179
 : Toutatis SERGEI PROKOFIEV Violin Concerto No.1 GUSTAV HOLST The Planets
 \n\nSources: Cape Cod Chamber\nEvent page: https://www.capecodchamber.org/
 event/cape-symphony%3a-the-planets/52409/
LOCATION:Cape Symphony\, 744 West Main St\, Hyannis\, MA\, 02601
URL:https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/cape-symphony%3a-the-planets/5240
 9/
END:VEVENT
