BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Colonial Faire and Muster of Fyfes and Drums
DTSTART:20260926T000000
DTEND:20260926T000000
DTSTAMP:20260923T155014Z
UID:9db1cc1bd3912018438abc04ba17c7@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Our 250th Independence Day has come and gone\, but the party c
 ontinues. Come celebrate New England’s revolutionary heritage as histori
 c Longfellow’s Wayside Inn hosts a Colonial Faire and Muster of Fyfes an
 d Drums. Step back in time and experience living historians demonstrating 
 life in Massachusetts circa 1775. From military drills to contradancing\, 
 weaving to blacksmithing\, as well as children’s activities including 18
 th century games\, training with members of the French 85th Regiment Saint
  Onge and even an opportunity to fire a cannon\, the Spirit of America goe
 s on. At 12:00 following a reading of the Declaration of Independence\, th
 e tolling of church bells\, as well as a musket and cannon salute will her
 ald the start of the Grand Parade. The air will become filled with the mus
 ic that helped inspire the cause of liberty\, as 25 fife and drum corps fr
 om all over the northeast featuring the Middlesex County Volunteers (pictu
 red) process their way to the muster field where they will give individual
  performances throughout the afternoon. You may find the music captivating
 \, but don’t forget to stroll the craft booths along merchants’ row an
 d grab a bite to eat at the food court before enjoying your favorite bever
 age at the Wayside 1716 Beer Garden overlooking the Faire grounds.\n\nSour
 ces: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https://www.meetboston.com/event/colonial-fa
 ire-and-muster-of-fyfes-and-drums/92823/
LOCATION:Longfellow's Wayside Inn\, Sudbury\, Longfellow's Wayside Inn htt
 p://www.sudburymuster.org/\, Sudbury\, MA\, 01776
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/colonial-faire-and-muster-of-fyfes-an
 d-drums/92823/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:COME FROM AWAY!
DTSTART:20260926T140000
DTEND:20260926T160000
DTSTAMP:20260923T155014Z
UID:5cdf6a736dc1b3a97014b6efc25f0a@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:COME FROM AWAY is a moving and uplifting musical based on the 
 true story of what happened in the small town of Gander\, Newfoundland\, o
 n September 11\, 2001. When 38 planes carrying nearly 7\,000 passengers we
 re unexpectedly diverted there\, the residents of this isolated community 
 opened their hearts and homes to the stranded travelers. What began as a d
 ay of global tragedy transformed into a powerful tale of compassion\, conn
 ection\, and humanity. With a vibrant\, folk-inspired score and a fast-pac
 ed\, ensemble-driven narrative\, COME FROM AWAY captures the tensions\, cu
 lture clashes\, and eventual camaraderie that unfolded over several unforg
 ettable days. This Tony® Award-winning musical celebrates the best of the
  human spirit and the extraordinary capacity for good in the face of crisi
 s.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/even
 t/come-from-away/2026-09-26/1/
LOCATION:North Shore Music Theatre\, Dunham Road 54\, Beverly\, MA\, 01915
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/come-from-away/2026-09-26/1/
END:VEVENT
