BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Slayyyter
DTSTART:20260926T000000
DTEND:20260929T000000
DTSTAMP:20260923T155014Z
UID:c366f2db97ff75ffcfd3faf7a3202d@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:From her breakthrough 2019 self-titled mixtape to her 2021 deb
 ut Troubled Paradise and 2023’s STARFUCKER \, SLAYYYTER proved herself t
 o be one of the great shape-shifters of our time\, taking the past\, prese
 nt\, and future of pop and twisting it to her will. Early successes — 
 “Daddy AF” went from viral hit making SLAYYYTER’s name online to sou
 ndtracking a key scene in the Oscar Best Picture winner Anora — fueled a
 ccolades from publications including Billboard \, Paper \, Variety \, Roll
 ing Stone \, Pitchfork\, and more\, while earning SLAYYYTER opening slots 
 with forebears like Tove Lo and Kesha. But even with all that\, SLAYYYTER 
 decided something wasn’t quite right. She decided to become who she was 
 all along\, underneath it all: the WOR$T GIRL IN AMERICA . SLAYYYTER’s t
 hird album is the most authentically her\, while also boasting her most fu
 lly realized creative direction yet. She revisited her upbringing in St. L
 ouis\, and decided to make “iPod music” — a free-for-all of feral pu
 nk\, corroded pop\, and raunchy rap — conjuring the “Midwest-core twea
 ker bar rat” characters of her youth. Early singles “BEAT UP CHANEL$\,
 ” “CANNIBALISM!\,” and “CRANK” steadily built hype for the proje
 ct over the course of 2025\, with fans fervently embracing the raw\, swagg
 ering Slayyyter that emerged from the ashes of her past selves. WOR$T GIRL
  IN AMERICA is both revelation and evolution\, killing the SLAYYYTER we th
 ought we knew so SLAYYYTER could be born for real.\n\nSources: Meet Boston
 \nEvent page: https://www.meetboston.com/event/slayyyter/93227/
LOCATION:Roadrunner\, 89 Guest Street Boston Landing\, Brighton\, MA\, 021
 35
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/slayyyter/93227/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sprouts Kids Club | American Flatbread Worcester
DTSTART:20260926T000000
DTEND:20270626T000000
DTSTAMP:20260923T155014Z
UID:3946b273b65900928831e6bca7c2f9@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:SPROUTS A Monthly Kids Club rooted in good food\, creativity\,
  play\, and community. American Flatbread's Kids Club takes place on the l
 ast Saturday of every month. See below for our monthly themes and general 
 information about the program September 26: Back-to-School Bash October 31
 : Spooktacular Bowling Party November 28: Turkey Trot Bowling December 26:
  Holiday Workshop ABOUT THE PROGRAM: Sprouts is a monthly Kids Club where 
 kids can create\, play\, and grow together. Each month features a new them
 ed experience with a hands on craft\, a special bowling activity\, and som
 ething fun to take home. From decorating pumpkins and holiday ornaments to
  scavenger hunts and summer celebrations\, there is always something new f
 or kids to look forward to. Every Sprouts event takes place on the last Sa
 turday of the month\, with dedicated time for kids to create and bowl afte
 r if they would like. 10:00–11:00 AM: Craft & Activity 11:00 AM: Venue O
 pens for regularly scheduled business and Bowling is available for reserva
 tion. Food and beverage purchases can be made at this time. Reservations f
 or bowling are encouraged. Kids receive a Sprouts membership card when the
 y join and earn a stamp for every monthly event they attend. Birthday Mont
 h Get a Sprouts Kids Club T-shirt + 50% off bowling for any birthday party
 . Must be used during the child’s birthday month. Grow With Us Attend 6 
 Events: Earn a free 1 hour of bowling Attend 12 Events: Celebrate your Bir
 thday with a free birthday party for up to 25 guests. This includes the re
 servation of 3 bowling lanes\, cheese pizza\, and pepperoni pizza. Must be
  used during the child’s birthday month\n\nSources: Discover Central Mas
 sachusetts\nEvent page: https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/sprouts-ki
 ds-club-%7c-american-flatbread-worcester/30834/
LOCATION:American Flatbread Worcester\, 85 Green St. Suite 100\, Worcester
 \, MA\, 01604
URL:https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/sprouts-kids-club-%7c-american
 -flatbread-worcester/30834/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Step Back in Time at Upton’s Revolutionary War Encampment
DTSTART:20260926T000000
DTEND:20260926T000000
DTSTAMP:20260923T155014Z
UID:7173fda8c73ea41fe3812bad6594f6@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:UPTON — Step back in time and discover what life was like du
 ring the American Revolution when a Revolutionary War encampment comes to 
 the Upton Town Common on Saturday\, October 17\, from 10 a.m. to 3:30 p.m.
  This immersive historical program will bring the Revolutionary era to lif
 e through authentic military drills\, period-accurate encampments\, demons
 trations\, music\, and opportunities to learn about the people and activit
 ies of the 18th century. Visitors will have the opportunity to observe aut
 hentic military drills performed by Revolutionary War reenactors and explo
 re period-accurate encampments while talking with knowledgeable historical
  interpreters about military life and the challenges faced by those who li
 ved during the era. The encampment will also highlight everyday life in th
 e 18th century. Demonstrations will include cider making and a Printing Re
 volution demonstration\, while visitors can learn about period tools\, cra
 fts\, and daily routines. Fife and Fiddle musicians will perform during th
 e event\, adding to the sights and sounds of the Revolutionary era. Feelin
 g hungry while exploring the encampment? Soul Cafe will be on hand selling
  refreshments and baked goods. As communities across the nation commemorat
 e the 250th anniversary of the American Revolution\, this special program 
 offers an opportunity for people of all ages to experience history in a pe
 rsonal and engaging way. Students\, families\, and history enthusiasts are
  encouraged to attend and interact with the interpreters throughout the da
 y. The event is sponsored by the Upton Historical Society\, with funding i
 n part from the Upton Cultural Council. Admission is free and open to the 
 public. Donations are gratefully accepted and will help support the Upton 
 Historical Society’s ongoing efforts to preserve and share Upton’s his
 tory. Bring the family to the Upton Town Common on October 17 and experien
 ce the sights\, sounds\, and activities of the Revolutionary era as histor
 y comes alive! Website: https://uptonmahistory.org/ Facebook: https://www.
 facebook.com/UptonHistoricalSociety\n\nSources: Discover Central Massachus
 etts\nEvent page: https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/step-back-in-tim
 e-at-upton%e2%80%99s-revolutionary-war-encampment/30781/
LOCATION:Upton Town Center\, 1 Main St\, Upton\, MA\, 01568
URL:https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/step-back-in-time-at-upton%e2%
 80%99s-revolutionary-war-encampment/30781/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Lute: A 400th Anniversary Tribute to John Dowland
DTSTART:20260926T000000
DTEND:20260926T000000
DTSTAMP:20260923T155014Z
UID:0017e2f25fcf7c3efcf371f0f4050e@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Arts Speak Performance Lecture Come to an extraordinary lute l
 ecture-performance by Paul O’Dette\, Professor of Lute and Director of E
 arly Music at the Eastman School of Music and Artistic Co-Director of the 
 Boston Early Music Festival. This afternoon will focus on the music of Joh
 n Dowland\, English Renaissance composer\, lutenist\, and singer\, and the
  400th anniversary of his death in 1626. Don't miss this opportunity to he
 ar Paul O’Dette\, “the clearest case of genius ever to touch his instr
 ument.” (Toronto Globe and Mail) Free admission for all. Info: 508-240-2
 400 | artsempoweringlife.org\n\nSources: Cape Cod Chamber\nEvent page: htt
 ps://www.capecodchamber.org/event/the-lute%3a-a-400th-anniversary-tribute-
 to-john-dowland/52129/
LOCATION:Arts Empowering Life Inc.\, Performing Arts Center 95 Southern Ea
 gle Cartway\, Brewster\, MA\, 02631
URL:https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/the-lute%3a-a-400th-anniversary-t
 ribute-to-john-dowland/52129/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Milk Carton Kids
DTSTART:20260926T000000
DTEND:20260926T000000
DTSTAMP:20260923T155014Z
UID:f42c606f1ba4dad088abb4a39e5b02@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:On their seventh studio album\, Lost Cause Lover Fool (due Apr
 il 24 on Far Cry/Thirty Tigers)\, The Milk Carton Kids offer nine songs th
 at\, more than ever\, invite listeners to lean in close and linger inside 
 the small moments the record quietly magnifies. When Los Angeles–based s
 inger-songwriters Kenneth Pattengale and Joey Ryan first emerged in 2011\,
  they did so with a sound as unassuming as their “marketing” plan. The
 y recorded their ten-song debut\, Prologue \, with just their two guitars 
 and two voices. They posted it online as a free download\, sending the lin
 k to friends via email. Even amidst the foot stomps and hand claps carryin
 g Folk into the mainstream\, hundreds of thousands of people managed to fi
 nd Prologue in that first year. From the beginning\, The Milk Carton Kids 
 were more interested in precision than volume.\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEv
 ent page: https://www.meetboston.com/event/the-milk-carton-kids/90266/
LOCATION:The Wilbur\, 246 Tremont Street\, Boston\, MA\, 02116
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/the-milk-carton-kids/90266/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The NAA invites you to the 25th Annual Art Auction Exhibition & Ev
 ent
DTSTART:20260926T110000
DTEND:20261028T170000
DTSTAMP:20260923T155014Z
UID:dd49f198508626ced9143f5d622b54@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Newburyport Art (NAA) invites artists\, members\, collectors\,
  friends\, and art lovers to gather for a celestial celebration of 25 year
 s of creativity\, connection\, and community. This year’s Art Auction ex
 hibition is on display from Wednesday\, September 2nd until Saturday\, Oct
 ober 3rd. A ticketed auction party will be held on Saturday\, October 3rd
 \, from 4-8pm. Over 160 artworks are available for online silent auction b
 idding now until October 3rd @6pm. In the downstairs Sargent Gallery\, the
  exhibit includes NAA Member Artwork featuring photography\, mixed media\,
  sculpture\, oil\, acrylic and more. Upstairs in the Hartson Gallery is th
 e Collector’s Collection – showcasing artwork donated from private col
 lections\, including work by notable artists such as Harold Feinstein\, Ca
 ra Weston\, and Carlos Mérida. For online bidding & tickets to our Octobe
 r 3rd party\, visit: Auctria.events./NewburyportArt25 Since 1948\, Newbury
 port Art has believed in the power of art to bring people together. For on
 e unforgettable event\, Saturday\, October 3rd\, from 4-8pm\, 65 Water Str
 eet will transform into a celebratory theme of a black\, white and silver 
 sky. The afternoon and evening offers a variety of ways to experience the 
 celebration including: live painting by Alan Bull and a chance to purchase
  his piece\; bidding on Members’ Artwork\, Collectors Collection\, and S
 ilent Auction Packages\; adding your own star and to an interactive commun
 ity constellation\; free tarot reading\; dancing to live jazz & swing with
  Jared Holaday\; sipping on a signature cocktail from the open bar\; enjoy
 ing catered food and dessert\; posing for your Moon Portrait in the sculpt
 ure garden\; and sharing your NAA story in an optional two-minute video in
 terview. NAA Member tickets: $70\; Non-member tickets: $90\; with a sugges
 ted attire of cosmic shine! Thank you to our lead sponsors\, Matter Commun
 ications\, Milestone 35 Tools & Woodworking\, and the Hylton Family Trust 
 for supporting our 25th Annual Art Auction. Gallery Hours: Wednesday throu
 gh Sunday from 11:00am–5:00pm. The gallery is handicap accessible. More 
 information\, as well as an online gallery is available at newburyportart.
 org.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/ev
 ent/the-naa-invites-you-to-the-25th-annual-art-auction-exhibition-event/20
 26-09-26/
LOCATION:Newburyport Art Association\, 65 Water St\, Newburyport\, MA\, 01
 950
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/the-naa-invites-you-to-the-25th-annual
 -art-auction-exhibition-event/2026-09-26/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Planets
DTSTART:20260926T000000
DTEND:20260927T000000
DTSTAMP:20260923T155014Z
UID:b8e0d6c5204afe9e64f7672694e535@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Date: September 26 & 27\, 2026 Showtimes: Sat 4:00 PM\, Sun 3:
 00 PM Featured Artist: Alyssa Wang\, Conductor Nathan Olson\, Violin Locat
 ion: Barnstable Performing Arts Center 744 West Main Street\, Hyannis\, MA
  02601 As we open a bold new season of discovery\, we invite you on a thri
 lling journey beyond the horizon. From the vastness of the cosmos to the w
 onder of the unknown\, this spectacular opening concert launches Worlds Aw
 ait with music that is thrilling\, cinematic\, and awe-inspiring. We’ll 
 begin in orbit\, with Kaija Saariaho’s radiant meditation on the motion 
 of the cosmos. Prokofiev’s Violin Concerto No. 1 follows\, balancing dre
 amlike lyricism with flashes of wit. The journey culminates in Holst’s T
 he Planets \, a suite of vivid astrological portraits from martial thunder
  to shimmering mysticism. Ticketholders are invited to an entertaining and
  informative talk about the concert program given by trombonist and schola
 r George Scharr beginning one hour before the performance.\n\nSources: Cap
 e Cod Chamber\nEvent page: https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/the-planet
 s/52364/
LOCATION:Barnstable Performing Arts Center 744 West Main Street\, Hyannis
URL:https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/the-planets/52364/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Sufi's Nightingale Musical
DTSTART:20260926T000000
DTEND:20260927T000000
DTSTAMP:20260923T155014Z
UID:202e42f8a03a4f60523664609da610@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:The historic Strand Theatre is proud to present the world-prem
 iere musical adaptation of Sarbpreet Singh’s acclaimed\, bestselling his
 torical novel\, The Sufi’s Nightingale. Written and composed by Singh\, 
 this queer-affirming production traces the extraordinary spiritual metamor
 phosis of Shah Hussain\, a 16th-century scholar who turns away from a rigi
 d seminary to become the celebrated “King of the Malamati Sufis” in me
 dieval Lahore. Told from the poignant perspective of Maqbool\, an intersex
  acolyte who serves as Hussain’s “nightingale\,” the narrative explo
 res the “unity of opposites”. When the handsome Brahmin youth Madho st
 orms into Hussain’s life\, it ignites a mesmerizing saga of passionate l
 ove\, jealousy\, and deep mystical devotion. Over time\, their individual 
 identities beautifully merge into folklore\, leaving a legacy that still c
 elebrates the ultimate triumph of love over law. The production features: 
 Live Musical Ensemble: Features brand-new\, original compositions by Sarbp
 reet Singh based on classical Ragas\, weaving together 16th-century spirit
 ual poetry (Kafis) by Shah Hussain\, Damodar Gulati\, and Raskhan. Mesmeri
 zing Choreography: Original choreography by accomplished Bharatanatyam dan
 cer Juhi Chaudhary\, beautifully blending traditional Sufi dancing\, Katha
 k\, ecstatic sama\, and dhamal dance. Timeless Relevance: A unique represe
 ntation of the rich culture of the Indian subcontinent that directly touch
 es on contemporary themes of universal love\, faith\, and the “othering
 ” of those outside societal norms. Performance Details Performance 1: Sa
 turday\, September 26\, 2026\, at 5:00 PM (Includes an exclusive post-show
  artist talkback with the writer/director and cast). Performance 2: Sunday
 \, September 27\, 2026\, at 2:00 PM. Runtime: Approx. 120 minutes. Admissi
 on: FREE to the public! Made possible through a Strand Theater Grant from 
 the City of Boston. Registration via Eventbrite is highly recommended to s
 ecure your seat. Critics’ Reviews of the Book “Historical fiction at i
 ts finest… one can almost feel the Sufi’s breath through the pages.”
  — Manu Pillai\, Sahitya Academy honoree and author “An extraordinary 
 effort that makes a reader relive history while simultaneously undertaking
  a spiritual journey of love in its purest form.” — Telegraph India 
 “Highlights the fault lines of caste\, gender\, and sexuality… to spre
 ad love.” — The Hindu About the Author and Composer Sarbpreet Singh is
  a Boston-based scholar-storyteller\, playwright\, and composer. He is the
  creator of the globally acclaimed Story of the Sikhs podcast and the auth
 or of several bestsellers. His previous stage production\, Kultar’s Mime
 \, toured six countries to critical acclaim\, and his recent cultural adap
 tations continue to enrich the Boston performing arts scene. Don’t miss 
 this spellbinding journey of music\, movement\, and transcendental love. R
 eserve your free tickets today!\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https
 ://www.meetboston.com/event/the-sufis-nightingale-musical/92625/
LOCATION:Strand Theater\, Dorchester\, Strand Theater 543 Columbia Road\, 
 Boston\, MA\, 02125
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/the-sufis-nightingale-musical/92625/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:"Wild & Tended" with Mary Mackenzie\, soprano and Matthew Jaskot\,
  piano
DTSTART:20260926T000000
DTEND:20260926T000000
DTSTAMP:20260923T155014Z
UID:f1b7b79ee9acd177e67330607088cb@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Art song was born as an intimate genre\, written to be perform
 ed in people’s homes — music for a room\, for a gathered circle of fri
 ends\, for a voice close enough to hear every detail. It continues to be a
  vibrant and diverse genre\, and this program lives in that tension — be
 tween the wild and the tended — tracing art song from its Romantic roots
  to music written in our own time. Featuring an array of songs by Clara Sc
 humann\, Hugo Wolf\, Arnold Schoenberg\, Lili Boulanger\, Francis Poulenc
 \, and American composers Charles Ives\, Aaron Copland\, Samuel Barber\, a
 nd John Frantzen. All events are free to those under 18. The Massachusetts
  Card To Culture covers all holders of a current EBT\, WIC\, or Commonweal
 th Connector Care Insurance card. Click on links for each card for more ge
 neral information about this program. Card holders may request up to two f
 ree tickets at the box office for any ticketed concert on the concert day
 \, or may make a reservation by email to events@friendsofthestonechurch.or
 g. Please include your name\, an email address or telephone number\, conce
 rt date and # of tickets being reserved in your request. About the Artists
  Critically acclaimed as “a soprano of extraordinary agility and concent
 ration” by The New York Times \, soprano Mary Mackenzie has emerged as o
 ne of contemporary music’s most compelling storytellers. With a career t
 hat has taken her to performances in 11 U.S. States and Washington D.C.\, 
 as well as a seasoned discography spanning eleven years\, Ms. Mackenzie is
  particularly known for her evocative chamber music performances. For her 
 efforts\, she has earned praise for a “sensational\, epically unsettling
 ” rendition of George Crumb by the Boston Globe and her “mystifying”
  vocal effects by The Financial Times . Examples of some of her most immer
 sive work to date includes several “one-woman” performances\, like the
  United States premiere of Héctor Parra’s monodrama H ypermusic: Ascens
 ion at the Guggenheim Museum\, a highly technological experience which uti
 lized Harvard professor of theoretical physics Lisa Randall as librettist.
  www.marymacksoprano.com Matthew Jaskot is a composer\, pianist\, organist
 \, concert curator\, and a professor of music at the College of the Holy C
 ross in Worcester\, MA where he teaches music theory\, composition\, and i
 s the collaborative pianist for the College Choir. Matt is a versatile pia
 nist who specializes in 20th and 21st century music\, while being equally 
 adept at performing traditional repertoire\, jazz\, and popular music. He 
 has performed nationally and internationally at various festivals and conf
 erences\, most recently as guest performer in the Ecce Ensemble\, premieri
 ng works at the Etchings Festival in Northampton\, MA. Last spring\, he or
 ganized a program\, featuring a two-piano performance of Stravinsky's Le S
 acre du Printemps\, with colleague Sonya Ovrutsky Fensome\, a collaborativ
 e concert with the dance department at Holy Cross. www.matthewjaskot.com\n
 \nSources: Discover Central Massachusetts\nEvent page: https://www.discove
 rcentralma.org/event/wild-%26-tended-with-mary-mackenzie-soprano-and-matth
 ew-jaskot-piano/30856/
LOCATION:Stone Church Cultural Center\, 283 Main Street\, Route 32\, Gilbe
 rtville\, MA\, 01031
URL:https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/wild-%26-tended-with-mary-mack
 enzie-soprano-and-matthew-jaskot-piano/30856/
END:VEVENT
