SUMMARY:Author Talk with Janis Robinson Daly at West Falmouth Library
DTSTART:20260927T000000
DTEND:20260927T000000
DTSTAMP:20260923T155014Z
UID:9becd5642604a5ff7e3f7fa76c57f8@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Author Talk with Janis Robinson Daly Join us at West Falmouth 
 Library Sunday\, September 27 at 4 p.m. for an engaging talk with Cape Cod
 \, award-winning historical fiction author Janis Robinson Daly as she shar
 es her inspiration and research which led to writing her latest novel Unde
 r Two Flags: a Novel of World War I. Free and open to all. Co-presented wi
 th Eight Cousins Bookstore. Drawing upon the memoir of eighteen-year-old J
 osephine Therese Marzynski\, a Boston opera student trapped in Berlin duri
 ng World War I\, Daly explores how Josephine’s passion for music drives 
 her strength to endure even in humanity’s darkest hours. Early praise hi
 ghlights Daly’s deft storytelling and emotional depth: “Daly sensitive
 ly explores war\, patriotism\, and ambition in this well-researched tale.
 ”— Kate Quinn\, bestselling author of The Alice Network Register Here
 \n\nSources: Cape Cod Chamber\nEvent page: https://www.capecodchamber.org/
 event/author-talk-with-janis-robinson-daly-at-west-falmouth-library/52324/
LOCATION:West Falmouth Library\, 575 West Falmouth Highway\, West Falmouth
 \, MA\, 02574
URL:https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/author-talk-with-janis-robinson-d
 aly-at-west-falmouth-library/52324/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Brazilian Festival of Worcester
DTSTART:20260927T000000
DTEND:20260927T000000
DTSTAMP:20260923T155014Z
UID:7e2042f8fb437e39594abf2859a199@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate the vibrant spirit of Brazil at the 7th Annual Brazi
 lian Festival of Worcester\, taking place on Sunday\, September 13\, 2026
 \, from 10:00 AM to 6:00 PM at Institute Park in Worcester\, Massachusetts
 . Held during the month of Brazil’s Independence\, the Brazilian Festiva
 l of Worcester brings the community together for a colorful celebration of
  Brazilian culture\, heritage\, music\, dance\, food\, arts\, and traditio
 ns. The festival is free and open to the public\, welcoming families and v
 isitors of all backgrounds to experience the warmth\, diversity\, and joyf
 ul spirit of Brazil right here in Central Massachusetts. This year’s fes
 tival will feature a special Tribute to Bahia\, one of Brazil’s most cul
 turally rich and historic states. Guests will have the opportunity to expe
 rience elements of Bahian culture alongside traditions representing differ
 ent regions of Brazil. Throughout the day\, Institute Park will come alive
  with live Brazilian music\, singers and musicians\, samba\, capoeira\, cu
 ltural dance performances\, rhythmic gymnastics\, and other special perfor
 mances. The festival will also feature a variety of food vendors offering 
 Brazilian favorites as well as international cuisine\, reflecting the mult
 icultural community that calls Worcester home. Families are especially wel
 come! Children can enjoy a variety of activities and entertainment\, inclu
 ding face painting\, character appearances\, pony rides\, games\, prizes\,
  and other family-friendly attractions. Visitors can also explore a divers
 e marketplace of local vendors\, small businesses\, entrepreneurs\, commun
 ity organizations\, sponsors\, and cultural partners\, making the festival
  an opportunity to celebrate culture while supporting businesses and organ
 izations from throughout the region. A special Civic Opening Ceremony at 1
 2:00 PM will bring together community leaders\, invited officials\, partne
 rs\, performers\, and members of the Brazilian-American community in recog
 nition of Brazilian Independence and the contributions of Brazilians to Wo
 rcester and Massachusetts. More than an event\, the Brazilian Festival of 
 Worcester is a celebration of community\, cultural diversity\, connection
 \, and Brazilian pride. Whether you are Brazilian\, love Brazilian culture
 \, or simply want to experience something new\, everyone is invited to joi
 n us for a day filled with music\, flavors\, traditions\, family fun\, and
  the contagious joy of Brazil. 🇧🇷 Brazilian Festival of Worcester 
 📅 Sunday\, September 13\, 2026 ⏰ 10:00 AM – 6:00 PM 📍 Institute 
 Park\, 140 Salisbury Street\, Worcester\, MA 🎟️ FREE ADMISSION – Ev
 eryone is welcome!\n\nSources: Discover Central Massachusetts\nEvent page:
  https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/brazilian-festival-of-worcester/3
 0826/
LOCATION:Institute Park\, Institute Park 126 Salisbury Street\, Worcester
 \, MA\, 01609
URL:https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/brazilian-festival-of-worceste
 r/30826/
END:VEVENT
