DTSTART:20260927T000000
DTEND:20260927T000000
DTSTAMP:20260923T155014Z
UID:ed500fe2bec6ba4cbd4841923a7766@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Area 9 Saxophone Quartet presents a program celebrating the br
 eadth of the Western classical tradition through the unique voice of the s
 axophone. Audiences will experience music spanning multiple centuries\, fr
 om elegant transcriptions of Baroque works to vibrant contemporary composi
 tions written for saxophone quartet. Blending familiar sounds with fresh d
 iscoveries\, the program offers an engaging look at the rich colors and ex
 pressive possibilities of the ensemble. Sean Mix\, Soprano Saxophone Cara 
 Hachten\, Alto Saxophone John Rabinowitz\, Tenor Saxophone Seychelle Dunn-
 Corbin\, Baritone Saxophone FPAC Harbor Harmonies 2026\, directed by class
 ical pianist Jane Hua\, in its 3rd season brings high quality concert musi
 c free admission to Boston residents and visitors. HH supports US trained
 \, foreign-born musical artists that are Greater Boston residents\, who ha
 ve demonstrated their dedication to artistic excellence through published 
 works\, critical acclaim\, and sustained career achievements. Thank you to
  The Boston Foundation for making this concert possible and accessible for
  all. MORE INFO / RSVP\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https://www.me
 etboston.com/event/harbor-harmonies-2026/92782/
LOCATION:FPAC Art Space\, FPAC Art Space 70A Sleeper Street\, Boston\, MA
 \, 02210
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/harbor-harmonies-2026/92782/
END:VEVENT
