BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Nashoba Valley Pride (Rescheduled)
DTSTART:20260927T000000
DTEND:20260927T000000
DTSTAMP:20260923T155014Z
UID:62c3cca18f3f022458bae043c87dc2@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate community\, inclusion\, and Pride at the 2026 Nashob
 a Valley Pride Celebration\, a free\, family- and kid-friendly event hoste
 d by the Nashoba Valley Pride Committee. This annual celebration brings to
 gether LGBTQ+ individuals\, families\, friends\, neighbors\, and allies fr
 om across the Nashoba Valley and beyond for an afternoon of connection\, v
 isibility\, education\, entertainment\, and fun in the heart of Bolton\, M
 assachusetts. The day begins with a community Pride Parade at 1:00 PM\, de
 parting from Emerson School\, traveling along Main Street\, and concluding
  at the Bolton Town Common\, where the Pride Festival continues until 4:00
  PM. Festival attendees can enjoy an exciting lineup of speakers\, drag pe
 rformances\, live music\, community organizations\, local vendors\, raffle
 s\, and a variety of food trucks. Visitors will also have the opportunity 
 to connect with LGBTQ+ organizations and local community groups that provi
 de education\, resources\, advocacy\, and support throughout the region. W
 hether you're attending with children\, meeting friends\, or simply lookin
 g to show your support as an ally\, Nashoba Valley Pride offers a welcomin
 g and inclusive atmosphere where everyone is encouraged to celebrate authe
 nticity\, respect\, and belonging. The event is free and open to the publi
 c. Schedule 1:00 PM: Pride Parade from Emerson School to the Bolton Town C
 ommon 1:30–4:00 PM: Festival on the Bolton Town Common Festival Highligh
 ts Community Pride Parade Inspiring speakers Drag performances Live music 
 LGBTQ+ organizations and community resources Local vendors Food trucks Raf
 fles Family-friendly activities and community celebration Parking Parking 
 is available at: Emerson School Florence Sawyer School First Parish Church
 \, 673 Main Street The event is ADA accessible. Follow @nashobavalleypride
  on Facebook and Instagram for updates\, announcements\, and additional ev
 ent information. More info is also available at https://tinyurl.com/nvpf20
 26. Come celebrate a vibrant\, welcoming community where everyone belongs!
 \n\nSources: Discover Central Massachusetts\nEvent page: https://www.disco
 vercentralma.org/event/nashoba-valley-pride-(rescheduled)/30461/
LOCATION:Bolton Town Common\, Bolton MA\, 100 Powdermill Road Suite 159\, 
 Acton\, MA\, 01720
URL:https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/nashoba-valley-pride-(reschedu
 led)/30461/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Newburyport Art honors “Through His Eyes: Celebrating Jay McCart
 hy”
DTSTART:20260927T110000
DTEND:20260927T170000
DTSTAMP:20260923T155014Z
UID:86db46349249909f04cc595b9c107d@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Newburyport Art (NAA): Through His Eyes is an exhibition celeb
 rating the work of photographer Jay McCarthy\, on view from Wednesday\, Se
 ptember 16th – Sunday\, September 27th. Jay was passionate about his cra
 ft of photography for over 50 years. Beginning with a love of film photogr
 aphy and slide work\, Jay specialized in landscape and portrait work\, but
  also found beauty in abstract and whimsical subjects. His award winning w
 ork has been shown in multiple galleries\, corporations\, and Institutions
 \, and hangs in homes around the country and abroad. A graduate of the Uni
 versity of Mass at Lowell\, Jay attended the New York Institute of Photogr
 aphy. Following retirement from Project Management work at Wang Corp\, Com
 pac\, and Fidelity\, Jay served as President of the Board of Directors at 
 Newburyport Art\, and thoroughly enjoyed his years working there as Galler
 y Associate and Moderator of the Photo Interest Group. He particularly enj
 oyed introducing photography classes to Veterans and young students as wel
 l. Jay was married to Nancy McCarthy who is hosting this exhibit. Inspired
  by Jay’s love of photography \, his children and grandchildren have beg
 un to follow in his creative footsteps.We lost our beloved Jay on January 
 18\, 2025\, and though he is deeply missed\, the poignant beauty he captur
 ed will continue to live on ‘Through His Eyes’. Please join Nancy McCa
 rthy in a celebration of Jay’s life through his photography\, including 
 a public\, cordial invite to the reception on Saturday\, September 19th fr
 om 4:00-6:00 PM The gallery and reception are free and open to the public 
 and all of Jay’s photographs are for sale. Gallery Hours: Wednesday thro
 ugh Sunday from 11am-5pm. The gallery is handicap accessible. More informa
 tion\, as well as an online gallery is available at newburyportart.org. Fo
 unded in 1948\, Newburyport Art is dedicated to promoting and exhibiting m
 embers’ work and to providing art education and access to the visual art
 s for the entire community.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https
 ://northofboston.org/event/newburyport-art-honors-through-his-eyes-celebra
 ting-jay-mccarthy/2026-09-27/
LOCATION:Newburyport Art Association\, 65 Water St\, Newburyport\, MA\, 01
 950
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/newburyport-art-honors-through-his-eye
 s-celebrating-jay-mccarthy/2026-09-27/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Newburyport Art presents May Exhibitions at 65 Water Street
DTSTART:20260927T110000
DTEND:20260927T170000
DTSTAMP:20260923T155014Z
UID:20e4ea9be6caa2f6a84bf8b9a39a57@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Newburyport Art (NAA) presents three new shows opening in the 
 month of May! Soft Structures is a group exhibition that explores fibers a
 nd fibrous material as process and metaphor. This exhibit features over 80
  artworks in a variety of media including drawing\, painting\, sculpture\,
  weaving\, embroidery\, quilting\, collage\, mixed media and more. This ex
 hibit is on view in the first-floor Sargent Gallery and second-floor Harts
 on Gallery. FOLIA is a collaborative exhibition featuring works by Amesbur
 y artists Amy Vander Els & Heather Karp. This exhibit explores the quiet b
 eauty and joyful rhythm of leaves and the symbolic meaning behind many tha
 t speaks of perseverance\, resilience and hope. Thirty-six artworks are di
 splayed amongst spring greenery in the first-floor Hills Gallery. Amy and 
 Heather will give a free artist talk on Thursday\, May 21st from 6:00-7:00
 pm\, concluding with Q&A. The 11th Annual Outdoor Sculpture Garden Exhibit
 ion debuted on May 1st\, and will remain on view year-round until April 20
 27. At nearly 3\,000 square feet\, the Range Lights Sculpture Garden resid
 es behind the historic NAA and is seen and visited by hundreds of people e
 very week. This year’s exhibition features 16 pieces by 10 local and reg
 ional artists. The participating artists include\; Jeffrey Briggs\, Lindle
 y Briggs\, Sarah Burns and Mike Platt\, Alexis Guieb-Alimbuyuguen\, Andrew
  Henschel\, Mae Kenny\, Evan Ralph\, Michael Updike and Raynor Warner. A r
 eception for FOLIA and Soft Structures will be held on Saturday\, May 2nd 
 from 4-6pm\, with the 11th Annual Sculpture Exhibit reception beginning at
  3:00pm\, including a Best in Show award at 3:30pm. The receptions are fre
 e and open to the public\, and visitors participating in the May 2nd Newbu
 ryport Artwalk are encouraged to stop by. New Hours: Wednesday through Sun
 day from 11:00am–5:00pm. The gallery is handicap accessible. More inform
 ation\, as well as an online gallery is available at newburyportart.org. F
 ounded in 1948\, Newburyport Art\, a 501(c)(3) non-profit\, is dedicated t
 o promoting and exhibiting members’ work and to providing art education 
 and access to the visual arts for the entire community. The gallery and ev
 ents are free and open to the public.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent p
 age: https://northofboston.org/event/newburyport-art-presents-may-exhibiti
 ons-at-65-water-street/2026-09-27/
LOCATION:Newburyport Art Association\, 65 Water St\, Newburyport\, MA\, 01
 950
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/newburyport-art-presents-may-exhibitio
 ns-at-65-water-street/2026-09-27/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Pat Metheny
DTSTART:20260927T000000
DTEND:20260927T000000
DTSTAMP:20260923T155014Z
UID:3d7d5337eca48c85bc5a55f8f89d22@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Pat Metheny\, born August 12\, 1954\, in Lee’s Summit\, Miss
 ouri\, has stood at the forefront of modern music for more than five decad
 es. Beginning on trumpet at age eight and switching to guitar at twelve\, 
 Metheny was performing with Kansas City’s top jazz musicians by fifteen
 —an early start that helped shape his unmistakable sound. After joining 
 vibraphonist Gary Burton’s group in 1974\, Metheny’s horn-like phrasin
 g\, lyrical touch\, and rhythmic fluidity quickly distinguished him. His d
 ebut album\, Bright Size Life (1975)\, redefined the possibilities of jazz
  guitar\, introducing a new sonic openness and melodic clarity that inspir
 ed generations of players. With more than 20 million albums sold and 20 Gr
 ammy Awards in ten different categories—a record unmatched by any other 
 artist—Metheny’s influence extends across genres and generations. His 
 collaborations span from Steve Reich and Ornette Coleman to Herbie Hancock
 \, Jim Hall\, Milton Nascimento\, and David Bowie. His compositions encomp
 ass everything from solo guitar works and orchestral pieces to the groundb
 reaking Orchestrion project. A dedicated educator\, Metheny became the you
 ngest instructor in the history of both the University of Miami and Berkle
 e College of Music\, where he later received an honorary doctorate. He is 
 a member of the DownBeat Hall of Fame\, a NEA Jazz Master\, and an inducte
 e of both the Royal Swedish Academy of Music and the Missouri Hall of Fame
 . In 2026\, Metheny will embark on a world tour with his new ensemble Side
 -Eye III+\, supporting the release of their self-titled album—the first 
 on his new label\, Uniquity Music\, which will encompass all of his record
 ings since 1984 and all future projects. Lineup: Joe Dyson - Drums Chris F
 ishman - Piano/Keyboards Jermaine Paul - Bass Leonard Patton - Percussion/
 Vocals\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https://www.meetboston.com/eve
 nt/pat-metheny/88970/
LOCATION:Chevalier Theatre\, 30 Forest Street\, Medford\, MA\, 02155
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/pat-metheny/88970/
END:VEVENT
