BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Kennedy Ryon
DTSTART:20260928T000000
DTEND:20260928T000000
DTSTAMP:20260923T155014Z
UID:9965e840d1d7a6a133fef1f03f1994@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:In 2025\, Kennedy Ryon sold more than 1\,500 tickets across he
 r first eight-city headline run\, a striking number for an artist without 
 a label backing the effort. Every date\, every stream\, every piece of the
  operation belongs to her and her small team. That ownership shows up in t
 he music itself: intimate\, unflinching songs built for solitary listening
  that somehow also ignite a room the moment the beat drops. It's an approa
 ch that has earned her over 600\,000 followers across platforms and close 
 to a quarter million monthly Spotify listeners\, all without the usual ind
 ustry machinery. Boston hosts her on The Can We Evolve? Tour\, her most am
 bitious headline run yet\, arriving alongside her forthcoming album "Can I
  Evolve?" Monthly single releases have built anticipation toward the full 
 album's February 2027 streaming debut\, most recently with "Beggin' and Ch
 oosin'." City Winery Boston's seated\, intimate room is where this music b
 elongs\, close enough to catch every nuance in her voice\, paired with che
 f-driven dishes and our in-house wines poured through the evening. It's a 
 setting built for exactly the kind of connection her songs are chasing. LE
 ARN MORE / GET TICKETS\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https://www.me
 etboston.com/event/kennedy-ryon/93095/
LOCATION:City Winery Boston\, City Winery 80 Beverly Street\, Boston\, MA
 \, 02114
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/kennedy-ryon/93095/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mortality Movies - Tender
DTSTART:20260928T000000
DTEND:20260928T000000
DTSTAMP:20260923T155014Z
UID:83534783a1ddc6c745f279ce3ff8db@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Join us at the Woods Hole Library for a death and dying film s
 creening and discussion series using films to foster open\, compassionate 
 community dialogue around end-of-life planning\, death\, dying\, post-deat
 h care\, and bereavement. This community-centered program seeks to help br
 eak cultural taboos and ease the fear of the unknown by bringing people to
 gether to share perspectives. Hosted by Cape Cod Community Death Education
 \, with discussion facilitated by Heather Massey\, Kyle Banks\, and others
  of the facilitation team. This is an in-person event. On Monday\, Septemb
 er 28\, at 3pm we will screen Tender. This documentary film is set against
  the stunning backdrop of the industrial seaside town of Port Kembla\, whe
 re a feisty and resilient community group have determined to take back the
  responsibility that most of us leave to someone else – to care for thei
 r own dead. Scattered throughout are stories that cut to the core revealin
 g why this small band have decided to take on a practice that for most is 
 taboo. As their plans for community-based funerals gather momentum one of 
 their own is diagnosed with a life-threatening illness. Tender is at once 
 a heartbreakingly beautiful and beautifully funny glimpse of an extraordin
 ary community taking on one of the most essential challenges of human life
 …its end.\n\nSources: Cape Cod Chamber\nEvent page: https://www.capecodc
 hamber.org/event/mortality-movies-tender/52493/
LOCATION:Woods Hole Public Library\, 581 Woods Hole Road\, Woods Hole\, MA
 \, 02543
URL:https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/mortality-movies-tender/52493/
END:VEVENT
