DESCRIPTION:4 Day Workshop One of the greatest challenges in kiln-formed g
 lass is capturing intricate detail in finished work. This hands-on worksho
 p introduces students to Non-Traditional Pâte de Verre techniques—an in
 novative approach to working with glass paste at low temperatures without 
 the use of investment molds. Students will learn how to recreate real or i
 magined objects in striking detail\, while also exploring methods that len
 d themselves to expressive abstraction. Dates: September 29 - October 2\, 
 2026 Meets: Tu\, W\, Th and F from 9:00 AM to 5:00 PM Location:25 Sagamore
