BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:26th Annual Heritage Award Celebration at Museums on the Green
DTSTART:20261001T000000
DTEND:20261001T000000
DTSTAMP:20260923T155014Z
UID:4099ac1c726448aa67528a96e04578@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:This October\, we are delighted to honor Tamsen Evans George w
 ith the Falmouth Historical Society’s 2026 Heritage Award\, celebrating 
 her extraordinary contributions to Falmouth’s history\, historic preserv
 ation\, the arts\, and the Museums on the Green. Tamsen’s connection to 
 Falmouth began when she was just eight years old\, and she has been an act
 ive member of our community for decades. Over the years\, she has served a
 s president of the Falmouth Historical Society for eight years\, volunteer
 ed as a docent and Collections Committee member\, helped strengthen our Fe
 deral furniture collection\, contributed to exhibitions and community prog
 rams\, and played an important role in the preservation and restoration of
  the Dr. Francis Wicks House. She was involved in the work of “Fix the W
 icks” long before it became the capital campaign we know today. Her comm
 itment to Falmouth extends well beyond the Museums\, including nearly a de
 cade of service on the Falmouth Historical Commission\, work with the Comm
 unity Preservation Committee\, and her recent involvement with the Falmout
 h 250th Committee. Her passion for history has also shaped her professiona
 l life and her writing. Tamsen has worked with organizations including the
  Cambridge Arts Council\, Massachusetts Cultural Council\, and Museum of F
 ine Arts\, where she served as Head of Public Programs. She later led two 
 nonprofit organizations and became deeply involved in historic restoration
 \, including the remarkable rehabilitation of historic properties and the 
 preservation of historic carriages. Following her retirement\, she turned 
 to historical writing\, authoring Allegiance\, The Life and Times of Willi
 am Eustis\, which was an award finalist in the United States History categ
 ory of American Book Fest\, as well as three eighteenth-century murder mys
 teries. Through all of this work\, Tamsen has shared a belief that history
  becomes most meaningful when we understand the real people behind it. Ple
 ase join us for an autumnal afternoon celebrating Tamsen and the remarkabl
 e legacy she has helped build in Falmouth. The celebration will take place
  in the Cultural Center at the Falmouth Museums on the Green\, a building 
 that holds a special place in Tamsen’s heart. The afternoon will include
  food and libations\, along with remarks from friends\, colleagues\, and c
 ommunity members who will share stories and highlight Tamsen’s many cont
 ributions to Falmouth and the Historical Society. Tickets are $50\, with p
 roceeds benefiting the Museum’s education and collections programs. We h
 ope you will join us in celebrating Tamsen and thanking her for the many w
 ays she has helped preserve\, strengthen\, and bring Falmouth’s history 
 to life. Register Here\n\nSources: Cape Cod Chamber\nEvent page: https://w
 ww.capecodchamber.org/event/26th-annual-heritage-award-celebration-at-muse
 ums-on-the-green/52486/
LOCATION:Falmouth Museums on the Green\, 55 & 65 Palmer Avenue\, Falmouth
 \, MA\, 02540
URL:https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/26th-annual-heritage-award-celebr
 ation-at-museums-on-the-green/52486/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Daily Guided & Self-Guided Tour of Hammond Castle Museum
DTSTART:20261001T090000
DTEND:20261001T153000
DTSTAMP:20260923T155014Z
UID:43911d79723e3bb3ac4115890a452b@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Step inside the breathtaking home of one of the most prolific 
 inventors of the 20th century\, John Hays Hammond\, Jr. Hammond Castle Mus
 eum is a dynamic STEAM museum\,*blending its historical significance as bo
 th **a historic house museum and a lapidarium. Inside\, you’ll not only 
 discover ancient\, medieval\, and Renaissance architectural elements and a
 rtifacts—including stone archways\, sarcophagi\, grave markers\, and an 
 extraordinary collection of stone and marble works—but you’ll also fin
 d a vibrant museum offering fresh educational and cultural arts programmin
 g. Visitors can explore items from the archival collection that have not b
 een publicly seen in generations\, along with newly curated content and th
 e most up-to-date information on the provenance of many pieces in our coll
 ection. New this season\, the Museum features four temporary exhibits that
  explore John Hays Hammond Jr. as both an individual and a scientific inno
 vator. In the Natalie Hays Hammond Temporary Exhibit Room\, Curatorial Dir
 ector John Leysath presents Spinning Platters with Hammond: Inside the Wor
 ld of Vinyl Records\, on display from April 29th through August 31st. Begi
 nning September 10th and running through the end of the 2025 season on Jan
 uary 4th\, Leysath will showcase” Hammond in Italy: The Love Affair Betw
 een the Hammonds & Italian Culture.”Additionally\, the Inventions Exhibi
 t Room will highlight Hammond’s groundbreaking Videotape Technology duri
 ng the spring and summer months\, followed by Hammond’s ahead-of-their-t
 ime Advertising Signs in the fall and early winter. Listed on the National
  Register of Historic Places\, and a repeated Reader’s Choice Best of No
 rth Shore winner by Northshore Magazine and a Trip Advisor Traveler’s Ch
 oice award recipient for the last three consecutive years\,** you can trus
 t that your visit will be an unforgettable experience. New This Season: Ne
 w Daily Hours and Flexible Arrival Times for Self-Guided Tours Open daily 
 from 9:00 am to 3:30 pm\, with the last entrance at 2:45 pm. The Museum\, 
 Museum Shop\, and grounds close at 3:30 pm. Experience Hammond Castle Muse
 um at your own pace with our new flexible arrival times for self-guided to
 urs. Your ticket grants you entry anytime within designated periods\, ensu
 ring you can arrive stress-free and enjoy your visit to the fullest. Morni
 ng Session: 9:00 am – 11:45 am / Afternoon Session: 11:45 am – 2:30 pm
  Self-guided tours allow you to explore at your own pace. We recommend pla
 nning for at least 60 minutes to experience the Museum’s fascinating gal
 leries\, grounds\, and temporary exhibits. **Accessibility Note: Please be
  aware that at nearly a century old\, the Hammond Castle Museum is not han
 dicapped accessible due to many difficult and winding stairs on the campus
  and within the Museum\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://no
 rthofboston.org/event/daily-guided-self-guided-tour-of-hammond-castle-muse
 um/2026-10-01/
LOCATION:Hammond Castle Museum\, 80 Hesperus Avenue\, Gloucester\, MA\, 01
 930
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/daily-guided-self-guided-tour-of-hammo
 nd-castle-museum/2026-10-01/
END:VEVENT
