BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Newburyport Art presents May Exhibitions at 65 Water Street
DTSTART:20261003T110000
DTEND:20261003T170000
DTSTAMP:20260923T155014Z
UID:98993ef5ee046c5bdc5dab9564fcc9@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Newburyport Art (NAA) presents three new shows opening in the 
 month of May! Soft Structures is a group exhibition that explores fibers a
 nd fibrous material as process and metaphor. This exhibit features over 80
  artworks in a variety of media including drawing\, painting\, sculpture\,
  weaving\, embroidery\, quilting\, collage\, mixed media and more. This ex
 hibit is on view in the first-floor Sargent Gallery and second-floor Harts
 on Gallery. FOLIA is a collaborative exhibition featuring works by Amesbur
 y artists Amy Vander Els & Heather Karp. This exhibit explores the quiet b
 eauty and joyful rhythm of leaves and the symbolic meaning behind many tha
 t speaks of perseverance\, resilience and hope. Thirty-six artworks are di
 splayed amongst spring greenery in the first-floor Hills Gallery. Amy and 
 Heather will give a free artist talk on Thursday\, May 21st from 6:00-7:00
 pm\, concluding with Q&A. The 11th Annual Outdoor Sculpture Garden Exhibit
 ion debuted on May 1st\, and will remain on view year-round until April 20
 27. At nearly 3\,000 square feet\, the Range Lights Sculpture Garden resid
 es behind the historic NAA and is seen and visited by hundreds of people e
 very week. This year’s exhibition features 16 pieces by 10 local and reg
 ional artists. The participating artists include\; Jeffrey Briggs\, Lindle
 y Briggs\, Sarah Burns and Mike Platt\, Alexis Guieb-Alimbuyuguen\, Andrew
  Henschel\, Mae Kenny\, Evan Ralph\, Michael Updike and Raynor Warner. A r
 eception for FOLIA and Soft Structures will be held on Saturday\, May 2nd 
 from 4-6pm\, with the 11th Annual Sculpture Exhibit reception beginning at
  3:00pm\, including a Best in Show award at 3:30pm. The receptions are fre
 e and open to the public\, and visitors participating in the May 2nd Newbu
 ryport Artwalk are encouraged to stop by. New Hours: Wednesday through Sun
 day from 11:00am–5:00pm. The gallery is handicap accessible. More inform
 ation\, as well as an online gallery is available at newburyportart.org. F
 ounded in 1948\, Newburyport Art\, a 501(c)(3) non-profit\, is dedicated t
 o promoting and exhibiting members’ work and to providing art education 
 and access to the visual arts for the entire community. The gallery and ev
 ents are free and open to the public.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent p
 age: https://northofboston.org/event/newburyport-art-presents-may-exhibiti
 ons-at-65-water-street/2026-10-03/
LOCATION:Newburyport Art Association\, 65 Water St\, Newburyport\, MA\, 01
 950
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/newburyport-art-presents-may-exhibitio
 ns-at-65-water-street/2026-10-03/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Newburyport Artwalk provides open studios and galleries!
DTSTART:20261003T100000
DTEND:20261003T170000
DTSTAMP:20260923T155014Z
UID:f39c8a2e1959ba9dfb7bb2e28f0c4c@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:The Newburyport ArtWalk is a FREE\, self-guided tour that enab
 les art enthusiasts to easily discover and explore Newburyport’s many wo
 nderful art galleries. This interactive art tour guides participants on an
  art adventure through Newburyport’s Historic District and also includes
  a few hidden gems just beyond downtown. In conjunction with the ArtWalk\,
  many local galleries showcase special exhibitions\, host engaging art dis
 cussions and live demonstrations of techniques. The 2026 ArtWalk will be h
 eld on Saturday\, Oct. 3rd from 10am-5pm. Participants are: Alan Bull Stud
 io\; Metzy’s Cantina\; CHALK Gallery\; Threadneedle Gallery\; Valerie’
 s Gallery \; Greetings by Design\; New England Sketch Book\; Newburyport A
 rt\; Blochaus Art Gallery\; The Galleryon Federal\; Chococoa Baking Co.\; 
 The Blue Lobster Print Studio and Gallery. Established in 2002 by a group 
 of independent art gallery owners\, the ArtWalk has showcased original fin
 e art cherished locally and respected throughout the national and internat
 ional artist communities. The Newburyport ArtWalk features a broad range o
 f art types and styles ranging from painting\, printmaking and sculpture t
 o artisan creations\, photography and ceramics. Whether you’re an artist
 \, a collector of fine art or an individual intrigued by art exploration\,
  the Newburyport ArtWalk is a wonderful opportunity to interact with and s
 upport the local artist community and discover new-found inspiration. ​ 
 While you’re enjoying the ArtWalk\, make sure to explore Newburyport’s
  many wonderful retail shops and relax at one of our many excellent local 
 Newburyport Restaurants. If you’re planning a visit from outside the are
 a\, consider booking a room in one of our wonderful local Inns. The Newbur
 yport ArtWalk events are funded by annual dues from the local participatin
 g art galleries. Please help support the local artist community by attendi
 ng the ArtWalk\, telling friends and family and by sharing on your social 
 media pages. Support Local!\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https
 ://northofboston.org/event/newburyport-artwalk-provides-open-studios-and-g
 alleries/
LOCATION:Newburyport Art Association\, 65 Water St\, Newburyport\, MA\, 01
 950
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/newburyport-artwalk-provides-open-stud
 ios-and-galleries/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Nicole Zuraitis Quartet
DTSTART:20261003T173000
DTEND:20261003T190000
DTSTAMP:20260923T155014Z
UID:84aceea55ab063219e825f41aa126c@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Nicole Zuraitis is a two-time Grammy-winning and six-time Gram
 my-nominated jazz singer-songwriter\, producer\, pianist\, arranger\, New 
 York-based bandleader and winner of the prestigious American Traditions Vo
 cal Competition Gold Medal. With a heart as big as her remarkable voice\, 
 ( Jazz Police )\, Nicole has positioned herself as one of the top artists 
 and prolific songwriters ( Broadway World ) to watch in jazz and beyond\, 
 or as she likes to call it\, The Modern Songbook.\n\nSources: The Berkshir
 es\nEvent page: https://berkshires.org/events-old/nicole-zuraitis-quartet/
LOCATION:Mahaiwe Performing Arts Center\, 14 Castle Street\, Great Barring
 ton\, MA\, 01230
URL:https://berkshires.org/events-old/nicole-zuraitis-quartet/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sinners\, Saints\, and Silent Souls: A Special Halloween Burying G
 round Walking Tour
DTSTART:20261003T000000
DTEND:20261031T000000
DTSTAMP:20260923T155014Z
UID:b543973b7fe82c6d6c014f453c8a3b@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Sinners\, Saints\, and Silent Souls: A Special Halloween Buryi
 ng Ground Walking Tour Saturdays in October! October 3rd\, 10th\, 17th\, 2
 4th\, & 31st\, at 3pm As Halloween approaches\, spirits come out of the sh
 adows\, eager to have their stories told. Now is the perfect time to visit
  them on their home turf. Join us for an enhanced Halloween version of our
  popular tour of Falmouth’s Old Burying Ground\, where we’ll explore t
 he gravesites of fascinating characters resting in the town’s oldest cem
 etery. In honor of the season\, we’ll also delve into spine-tingling tal
 es of alleged witches\, demons\, murder\, and monsters—all grounded in a
 ctual local history from our archives with a Falmouth twist. Falmouth has 
 a spooky side—come and see it for yourself! Whether you’ve joined us b
 efore or this is your first time\, you haven’t experienced a tour like t
 his. Parking: Please park in the lot at 157 Locust Street (bike path parki
 ng lot). Use the crosswalk to cross Locust St. and head toward the large b
 oulder of the Mariners’ Memorial. Opposite the Memorial\, across Mill Rd
 .\, join your tour guide at the top of Cemetery Lane. Recommended for ages
  13+ and those who can navigate uneven terrain. Meeting Point: The Old Bur
 ying Ground tour begins at the top of Cemetery Lane. Don’t forget to wea
 r long clothing\, bring bug spray\, and prepare for a hauntingly good time
 ! $30 General Admission\, $20 for Museums on the Green members — limit o
 f 20 people per walk\, pre-registration required Register Here\n\nSources:
  Cape Cod Chamber\nEvent page: https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/sinner
 s-saints-and-silent-souls%3a-a-special-halloween-burying-ground-walking-to
 ur/52487/
LOCATION:Falmouth Museums on the Green\, 55 & 65 Palmer Avenue\, Falmouth
 \, MA\, 02540
URL:https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/sinners-saints-and-silent-souls%3
 a-a-special-halloween-burying-ground-walking-tour/52487/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sons Of Cream
DTSTART:20261003T000000
DTEND:20261003T000000
DTSTAMP:20260923T155014Z
UID:d7f4181d22728eb30fe57a1860002c@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:The band Cream were one of the first supergroups\, blending th
 eir beloved blues with powerful rock licks and rhythms. Now\, nearly 60 ye
 ars after the trio of Eric Clapton\, Ginger Baker and Jack Bruce burst ont
 o the scene\, Payomet welcomes the new generation - Sons Of Cream. Celebra
 ting the iconic music of their fathers\, Ginger’s son Kofi and Jack’s 
 son Malcolm are joined by Ginger’s great nephew Rob Johnson. Having rece
 ntly signed to Marshall Records\, they will release their album ‘Half an
 d Half’ in early 2027. As the name suggests the record is a mix of Cream
  classics and original material that goes beyond the conventional blues-ro
 ck idiom. Quite simply\, it’s a not-to-be-missed night of blistering\, e
 xploratory songs and improvisation stemming from the legacy of their fathe
 rs..\n\nSources: Cape Cod Chamber\nEvent page: https://www.capecodchamber.
 org/event/sons-of-cream/52318/
LOCATION:Payomet Performing Arts Center\, 29 Old Dewline Road\, Truro\, MA
 \, 02666
URL:https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/sons-of-cream/52318/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The NAA invites you to the 25th Annual Art Auction Exhibition & Ev
 ent
DTSTART:20261003T110000
DTEND:20261104T160000
DTSTAMP:20260923T155014Z
UID:19f2b68a071370bbe2c664a2506c03@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Newburyport Art (NAA) invites artists\, members\, collectors\,
  friends\, and art lovers to gather for a celestial celebration of 25 year
 s of creativity\, connection\, and community. This year’s Art Auction ex
 hibition is on display from Wednesday\, September 2nd until Saturday\, Oct
 ober 3rd. A ticketed auction party will be held on Saturday\, October 3rd
 \, from 4-8pm. Over 160 artworks are available for online silent auction b
 idding now until October 3rd @6pm. In the downstairs Sargent Gallery\, the
  exhibit includes NAA Member Artwork featuring photography\, mixed media\,
  sculpture\, oil\, acrylic and more. Upstairs in the Hartson Gallery is th
 e Collector’s Collection – showcasing artwork donated from private col
 lections\, including work by notable artists such as Harold Feinstein\, Ca
 ra Weston\, and Carlos Mérida. For online bidding & tickets to our Octobe
 r 3rd party\, visit: Auctria.events./NewburyportArt25 Since 1948\, Newbury
 port Art has believed in the power of art to bring people together. For on
 e unforgettable event\, Saturday\, October 3rd\, from 4-8pm\, 65 Water Str
 eet will transform into a celebratory theme of a black\, white and silver 
 sky. The afternoon and evening offers a variety of ways to experience the 
 celebration including: live painting by Alan Bull and a chance to purchase
  his piece\; bidding on Members’ Artwork\, Collectors Collection\, and S
 ilent Auction Packages\; adding your own star and to an interactive commun
 ity constellation\; free tarot reading\; dancing to live jazz & swing with
  Jared Holaday\; sipping on a signature cocktail from the open bar\; enjoy
 ing catered food and dessert\; posing for your Moon Portrait in the sculpt
 ure garden\; and sharing your NAA story in an optional two-minute video in
 terview. NAA Member tickets: $70\; Non-member tickets: $90\; with a sugges
 ted attire of cosmic shine! Thank you to our lead sponsors\, Matter Commun
 ications\, Milestone 35 Tools & Woodworking\, and the Hylton Family Trust 
 for supporting our 25th Annual Art Auction. Gallery Hours: Wednesday throu
 gh Sunday from 11:00am–5:00pm. The gallery is handicap accessible. More 
 information\, as well as an online gallery is available at newburyportart.
 org.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/ev
 ent/the-naa-invites-you-to-the-25th-annual-art-auction-exhibition-event/20
 26-10-03/1/
LOCATION:Newburyport Art Association\, 65 Water St\, Newburyport\, MA\, 01
 950
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/the-naa-invites-you-to-the-25th-annual
 -art-auction-exhibition-event/2026-10-03/1/
END:VEVENT
