BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Raul Midon at The Mahaiwe
DTSTART:20261010T173000
DTEND:20261010T190000
DTSTAMP:20260923T155014Z
UID:f4b047d17251b07ed8e1b1244dc5e2@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Grammy-nominated singer-songwriter and guitarist Raul Midón h
 as built a genre-defying career that blends soul\, jazz\, Latin rhythms\, 
 and acoustic virtuosity into a sound entirely his own. Blind since birth\,
  Midón has often been described as a one-man band – turning his guitar 
 into an orchestra and his voice into a chorus ( The New York Times ). His 
 artistry has earned praise from icons such as Quincy Jones (his music make
 s you smile)\, Elton John (who called State of Mind a soul classic)\, and 
 Bill Withers\, who championed his music.\n\nSources: The Berkshires\nEvent
  page: https://berkshires.org/events-old/raul-midon-at-the-mahaiwe/
LOCATION:Mahaiwe Performing Arts Center\, 14 Castle Street\, Great Barring
 ton\, MA\, 01230
URL:https://berkshires.org/events-old/raul-midon-at-the-mahaiwe/
