BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Woods Hole Film Festival Dinner & A Movie: Beyond the Duplex Plane
 t
DTSTART:20261017T000000
DTEND:20261017T000000
DTSTAMP:20260923T155014Z
UID:208d52e167113c7e7bce109d5154c1@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Beyond the Duplex Planet In 1979\, David Greenberger\, a recen
 t art school grad became activities director at a Boston nursing home. Dav
 id began interviewing the residents\, rejecting pat questions with the une
 xpected: "Which do you prefer – coffee or meat?\," “What is embarrassm
 ent?\,” and “How close can you get to a penguin?” The result was The
  Duplex Planet\, an early ‘zine characterized by humor\, warmth and sinc
 erity. Today David’s work takes the form of spoken word shows and record
 ings. Beyond the Duplex Planet explores notions of aging and its intersect
 ion with art and community. It’s also a slightly ironic look at the life
  of an artist devoted to documenting the elderly who is himself in his sen
 ior years. Buy Tickets HERE. DINNER & A MOVIE is a film series presented b
 y Woods Hole Film Festival as part of its year-round independent film prog
 ram\, featuring twice-monthly screenings of independent films from early f
 all to late spring. The Dinner and a Movie series includes films from the 
 Woods Hole Film Festival\, as well as independent films curated specifical
 ly for the series. ABOUT THE SCREENINGS: Dinner and a Movie screenings are
  held at the Woods Hole Oceanographic Institution’s Redfield Auditorium.
  Screenings typically begin at 7:00 pm\, with doors opening for seating th
 irty minutes prior. Redfield Auditorium is located at 45 Water Street in W
 oods Hole. The facility is wheelchair accessible. Hearing assistance devic
 es are available at the venue\, upon request. Street parking is available 
 in Woods Hole. Free parking is available in certain lots operated by the W
 oods Hole Oceanographic Institution after 5 pm. ABOUT THE DINNER: Ticketho
 lders receive a discount at the Captain Kidd Restaurant & Quahog Republic 
 Leeside Pub. Reservations are encouraged. The Captain Kidd Restaurant at 7
 7 Water Street offers Dinner and a Movie ticket holders a 10% discount on 
 the meal portion (excluding any alcohol) of their bill. For reservations f
 or parties up to eight people\, please complete the online reservation for
 m and in the “special request” field\, please indicate Dinner and a Mo
 vie. This will help the staff accommodate the timing for the screening sta
 rt. For parties of nine or more\, please call 508-548-8563. Please note: T
 he Captain Kidd restaurant is closed seasonally from late December\, 2026 
 until late April\, 2027. Please contact the participating restaurant for r
 eservations or information. Ticket purchasers are asked to notify the rest
 aurant that they are attending the Dinner and A Movie screening upon seati
 ng\, and present their e-tickets for the discount or special offers.\n\nSo
 urces: Cape Cod Chamber\nEvent page: https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/
 woods-hole-film-festival-dinner-%26-a-movie%3a-beyond-the-duplex-planet/52
 431/
LOCATION:Woods Hole Oceanographic Institution\, Redfield Auditorium at WHO
 I 45 Water Street\, Woods Hole\, MA\, 02563
URL:https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/woods-hole-film-festival-dinner-%
 26-a-movie%3a-beyond-the-duplex-planet/52431/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Yin Yu Tang: A Chinese Home Tour
DTSTART:20261017T111500
DTEND:20261017T161500
DTSTAMP:20260923T155014Z
UID:20d6f54d9eb11afdc2c1bb4875b1d2@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Step inside a 200-year-old Chinese home in Salem to experience
  Chinese art\, architecture and culture. For 200 years\, Yin Yu Tang stood
  in the rural village of Huang Cun in a mountainous region of southeastern
  China. Home to eight generations of the Huang family\, this house was dis
 mantled\, transported and re-erected at the Peabody Essex Museum in 2003 t
 hrough a partnership between PEM and the governmental authorities of Huizh
 ou\, in Anhui Province. Yin Yu Tang’s journey constitutes a landmark col
 laboration between Chinese and American architects\, artisans\, conservato
 rs\, engineers and museum experts. The home is presented as it was when th
 e family last lived there in 1982. Plan Your Visit Exercise care Please he
 lp us preserve the house for future generations by refraining from touchin
 g objects and the structure itself. Non-flash photography and videography 
 is permitted for personal use only. Tripods and selfie sticks are not allo
 wed. Please walk with care and watch out for uneven stonework and raised t
 hresholds. Store your belongings\, but keep your coat Yin Yu Tang is parti
 ally outdoors and may be cool in fall and winter. Strollers\, bags\, backp
 acks and umbrellas are not permitted in the house. Please leave them at th
 e coatroom or the cubbies by the Information desk. Our staff at the entran
 ce of the house can look after strollers. Pick up your audio guide in adva
 nce Please pick up your complimentary audio guide\, available in English a
 nd Mandarin\, at the Information desk 10 minutes before your visit. Please
  note: Plan to bring your own pair of headphones. Before your visit\, pres
 s #50 to listen to an introduction to the house. Once inside\, look for st
 one blocks with two-digit numbers. Press the number plus the play > button
  to hear the audio. Be prompt Please be at the doors to Yin Yu Tang five m
 inutes before your scheduled visit with your audio guide in hand. A staff 
 member will alert you shortly before the end of your time slot.\n\nSources
 : North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/event/yin-yu-tang
 -a-chinese-home-tour/2026-10-17/
LOCATION:Peabody Essex Museum\, East India Square\, 161 Essex Street\, Sal
 em\, MA\, 01970
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/yin-yu-tang-a-chinese-home-tour/2026-1
 0-17/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
